 A vulnerability exists in the opexe_0 function within plug-ins/script-fu/tinyscheme/scheme.c. This bug, classified as CWE-120, can be triggered by processing a specially crafted input, leading to a buffer overflow. The overflow occurs because a buffer copy operation does not validate the size of the source data, allowing an out-of-bounds write that can corrupt memory and potentially lead to arbitrary code execution.
