[Mandatory] ID:
CVE-2021-46822

[Mandatory] Title: CVE-2021-46822 / CWE-787:
NA

[Optional] Disclosure / Patch Dates:
NA

[Optional] Affected products/versions:
NA

The Vulnerability
[Optional] CWE/CVE Number and description:
CWE-787 / CVE-2021-46822: NA
[Mandatory] Summary:
A vulnerability exists in the `get_word_rgb_row` function within `rdppm.c`. When processing a specially crafted 16-bit PPM file, the function can write past the boundaries of an allocated buffer due to incorrect pointer arithmetic that does not account for the output color space layout. This out-of-bounds write, as noted in the commit message, can lead to a segmentation fault.
[Mandatory] Root cause:
The root cause is the use of sequential pointer writes (`*ptr++`) without accounting for the destination buffer's pixel format and stride, leading to an out-of-bounds write.
[Mandatory] Attack Surface:
