[Mandatory] ID:
CVE-2014-125019

[Mandatory] Title: CVE-2014-125019 / CWE-787:
Out-of-bounds write in HEVC NAL unit processing

[Optional] Disclosure / Patch Dates:
Initial advisory: Not available in input — Patch release: Not available in input

[Optional] Affected products/versions:
Not available in input

The Vulnerability
[Optional] CWE/CVE Number and description:
CWE-787: Out-of-bounds Write
[Mandatory] Summary:
The vulnerability exists in the `decode_nal_unit` function within `libavcodec/hevc.c`. The function processes HEVC NAL units but fails to verify that all VCL NAL units within a frame have the same type. An attacker can trigger this condition by crafting a video file with mismatched NAL types, leading to an invalid memory access and potentially an out-of-bounds write during slice processing.
[Mandatory] Root cause:
The function lacks a check to ensure all VCL NAL unit types within a single frame are identical.
[Mandatory] Attack Surface:
Media player or transcoder using FFmpeg to process HEVC video files.
[Mandatory] Impact Summary:
Denial of Service via invalid memory access.
[Optional] Trigger / Attack vector:
A specially crafted HEVC video file.
[Mandatory] Key code/struct excerpt (minimal):

```c
        if (s->sh.first_slice_in_pic_flag) {
            ret = hevc_frame_start(s);
            if (ret < 0)
                return ret;
        } else if (!s->ref) {
            av_log(s->avctx, AV_LOG_ERROR, "First slice in a frame missing.\n");
            return AVERROR_INVALIDDATA;
        }

        if (!s->sh.dependent_slice_segment_flag &&
            s->sh.slice_type != I_SLICE) {
            ret = ff_hevc_slice_rpl(s);
            if (ret < 0) {
                av_log(s->avctx, AV_LOG_WARNING,
                       "Error constructing the reference lists for the current slice.\n");
                if (s->avctx->err_recognition & AV_EF_EXPLODE)
                    return ret;
            }
        }

        ctb_addr_ts = hls_slice_data(s);
```

Exploit:

[Mandatory] Trigger surface/attack vector:
File format (HEVC video file)

[Mandatory] Exploit primitive(s) available:
Invalid memory access, potential out-of-bounds write.

[Mandatory] Exploitability summary (1 sentence):
An attacker can create a malicious HEVC file that, when decoded, triggers the vulnerability due to a lack of type consistency checks.

[Mandatory] Exploit script (summary, 3—6 bullets):
- Create a HEVC bitstream containing a frame with multiple slices.
- Ensure the NAL unit type of the first slice differs from a subsequent slice.
- For example, the first slice could be a trailing slice (NAL_TRAIL_N) and a subsequent slice could be a random access slice (NAL_RADL_N).
- Serve the crafted file to an application using the vulnerable FFmpeg library.
- The `decode_nal_unit` function will process the mismatched slice types without validation.
- This leads to an invalid memory access when processing slice data.

Fix
[Mandatory] Fix code:
```c
        if (s->sh.first_slice_in_pic_flag) {
            ret = hevc_frame_start(s);
            if (ret < 0)
                return ret;
        } else if (!s->ref) {
            av_log(s->avctx, AV_LOG_ERROR, "First slice in a frame missing.\n");
            return AVERROR_INVALIDDATA;
        }

        if (s->nal_unit_type != s->first_nal_type) {
            av_log(s->avctx, AV_LOG_ERROR,
                   "Non-matching NAL types of the VCL NALUs: %d %d\n",
                   s->first_nal_type, s->nal_unit_type);
            return AVERROR_INVALIDDATA;
        }

        if (!s->sh.dependent_slice_segment_flag &&
            s->sh.slice_type != I_SLICE) {
            ret = ff_hevc_slice_rpl(s);
            if (ret < 0) {
                av_log(s->avctx, AV_LOG_WARNING,
                       "Error constructing the reference lists for the current slice.\n");
                if (s->avctx->err_recognition & AV_EF_EXPLODE)
                    return ret;
            }
        }

        ctb_addr_ts = hls_slice_data(s);
```

[Mandatory] Fix summary:
The patch adds a check to ensure that the NAL unit type of the current slice matches the type of the first slice in the picture. If they do not match, the function logs an error and returns `AVERROR_INVALIDDATA` to prevent further processing.

[Optional] Patch reference:
Commit b25e84b7399bd91605596b67d761d3464dbe8a6e

[Optional] Patch Analysis:
What did the fix do?
- Field: PatchType: Logic change (bounds check added)
[Optional] Variant & Triage Guidance

[Optional] Variant analysis suggestions (2—3 bullets):
- Review other multimedia parsers in FFmpeg for similar assumptions about data consistency across related segments.
- Fuzz the HEVC decoder with a focus on creating frames with mismatched NAL unit types.
- Check for other locations where slice segment properties are used without verifying consistency with the first slice.

[Optional] Likely variants/impact (one line):
Similar vulnerabilities could exist in other parts of the HEVC decoder or other codecs that assume consistency across related data units.

