[Mandatory] ID:
CVE-2022-2125

[Mandatory] Title: CVE-2022-2125 / CWE-122:
lisp indenting heap-based buffer overflow

[Optional] Disclosure / Patch Dates:
Initial advisory: 2022-06-19 — Patch release: 2022-06-17

[Optional] Affected products/versions:
vim before 8.2.5122

The Vulnerability
[Optional] CWE/CVE Number and description:
 Heap-based Buffer Overflow
[Mandatory] Summary:
 A heap-based buffer overflow exists in the `get_lisp_indent` function in `src/indent.c`. While parsing a line for lisp indentation, the code can read past the end of a string after processing escaped characters within a quoted string, leading to an out-of-bounds read. This is triggered by opening a specially crafted file in vim that contains specific lisp-like constructs.
[Mandatory] Root cause:
 Failure to check for NUL terminator in a string parsing loop.
[Mandatory] Attack Surface:
Local file open
[Mandatory] Impact Summary:
Potential arbitrary code execution
[Optional] Trigger / Attack vector:
 Opening a specially crafted file containing lisp code.
[Mandatory] Key code/struct excerpt (minimal):
if (*that == '\"' && *(that + 1) != NUL)
{
    while (*++that && *that != '\"')
    {
	// skipping escaped characters in the string
	if (*that == '\\')
	{
	    if (*++that == NUL)
		break;
	    if (that[1] == NUL)
	    {
		++that;
		break;
	    }
	}
    }
}

Exploit:

[Mandatory] Trigger surface/attack vector:
Local file open

[Mandatory] Exploit primitive(s) available:
Heap out-of-bounds read

[Mandatory] Exploitability summary (1 sentence):
Exploitable by opening a malicious file; difficulty depends on heap layout and subsequent use of read data.

[Mandatory] Exploit script (summary, 3—6 bullets):
Not available in input

Fix
[Mandatory] Fix code:
if (*that == '\"' && *(that + 1) != NUL)
{
    while (*++that && *that != '\"')
    {
	// skipping escaped characters in the string
	if (*that == '\\')
	{
	    if (*++that == NUL)
		break;
	    if (that[1] == NUL)
	    {
		++that;
		break;
	    }
	}
    }
    if (*that == NUL)
	break;
}

[Mandatory] Fix summary:
 Added a check for the NUL character after processing escaped strings to prevent the main loop from reading past the end of the line.
[Optional] Patch reference:
 https://github.com/vim/vim/commit/0e8e938d497260dd57be67b4966cb27a5f72376f
[Optional] Patch Analysis:
What did the fix do?
- Field: PatchType (e.g., bounds check added, logic refactor, feature removal)
bounds check added
[Optional] Variant & Triage Guidance

[Optional] Variant analysis suggestions (2—3 bullets):
- Review other functions in `src/indent.c` and related parts of the codebase for similar string parsing loops that may lack NUL terminator checks.
- Fuzz vim with various file types, especially those triggering complex indentation logic, to find similar over-read bugs.
- Audit the `ml_get_curline()` usage patterns to ensure all callers correctly handle the returned string.

[Optional] Likely variants/impact (one line):
Similar out-of-bounds reads could exist in other text processing or indentation routines.

