[Mandatory] ID:
CVE-2022-2175

[Mandatory] Title: CVE-2022-2175 / CWE-125: NA

[Optional] Disclosure / Patch Dates:
Initial advisory: 2022-06-23 — Patch release: 2022-06-22

[Optional] Affected products/versions:
vim < 8.2.5148

The Vulnerability
[Optional] CWE/CVE Number and description:
CWE-125: Out-of-bounds Read
[Mandatory] Summary:
The vulnerability exists in the `cmdline_insert_reg` function within `src/ex_getln.c`. When using an expression on the command line, the `new_cmdpos` variable is modified without saving its original state. This can lead to an invalid memory access after the operation, as the position may be left in an unexpected state, potentially causing an out-of-bounds read.
[Mandatory] Root cause:
The `new_cmdpos` global variable is modified without being saved and restored, potentially allowing it to reach an invalid state before being used as an index.
[Mandatory] Attack Surface:
vim command-line interface
[Mandatory] Impact Summary:
Potential information disclosure and application crash (DoS)
[Optional] Trigger / Attack vector:
vim command-line expression (e.g., <C-R>=)
[Mandatory] Key code/struct excerpt (minimal):
