[Mandatory] Fix summary:
The patch saves the original value of the `new_cmdpos` variable at the start of the function and restores it before returning. This prevents the position from being left in an invalid state after expression evaluation.

[Optional] Patch reference:
https://github.com/vim/vim/commit/6046aded8da002b08d380db29de2ba0268b6616e
[Optional] Patch Analysis:
The fix refactors the function to correctly preserve the state of the global `new_cmdpos` variable by saving its value on entry and restoring it on exit.
