[Mandatory] ID:
CVE-2022-2078

[Mandatory] Title: CVE-2022-2078 / CWE-121: NA
[Optional] Disclosure / Patch Dates:
Initial advisory: 2022-06-30 — Patch release: 2022-05-27

[Optional] Affected products/versions:
Linux kernel (from commit f3a2181e16f1 to before fecf31ee395b0295f2d7260aa29946b7605f7c85)

The Vulnerability
[Optional] CWE/CVE Number and description:
CWE-121 (Stack-based Buffer Overflow) / CVE-2022-2078
[Mandatory] Summary:
A vulnerability exists in the `nft_set_desc_concat_parse` function within the Linux kernel's netfilter subsystem. When processing netlink attributes to define a concatenated set, the function fails to check if the `field_count` has reached the bounds of the `field_len` array before incrementing it and writing a new length. This allows an attacker to write past the end of the `field_len` array, leading to a buffer overflow.
[Mandatory] Root cause:
Unchecked increment of `desc->field_count` allows an out-of-bounds write to the `desc->field_len` array.
[Mandatory] Attack Surface:
netfilter netlink interface (local configuration)
[Mandatory] Impact Summary:
Local Denial of Service (DoS)
[Optional] Trigger / Attack vector:
Specially crafted netlink message to nf_tables.
[Mandatory] Key code/struct excerpt (minimal):
```c
static int nft_set_desc_concat_parse(const struct nlattr *attr,
				     struct nft_set_desc *desc)
{
	struct nlattr *tb[NFTA_SET_FIELD_MAX + 1];
	u32 len;
	int err;

	err = nla_parse_nested_deprecated(tb, NFTA_SET_FIELD_MAX, attr,
					  nft_concat_policy, NULL);
	if (err < 0)
		return err;

	if (!tb[NFTA_SET_FIELD_LEN])
		return -EINVAL;

	len = ntohl(nla_get_be32(tb[NFTA_SET_FIELD_LEN]));
	if (len * BITS_PER_BYTE / 32 > NFT_REG32_COUNT)
		return -E2BIG;

	desc->field_len[desc->field_count++] = len;

	return 0;
}
```
