The Vulnerability
[Optional] CWE/CVE Number and description:
 Out-of-bounds Read
[Mandatory] Summary:
 A bug exists in the `X86_insn_reg_intel` function within `arch/X86/X86Mapping.c`. The binary search implementation incorrectly calculates the `mid` index at the end of the loop iteration instead of the beginning. This can cause `insn_regs_intel_sorted[mid]` to be accessed with an out-of-bounds index, leading to an out-of-bounds read.
[Mandatory] Root cause:
 Incorrect calculation of the `mid` variable in the binary search loop, leading to an out-of-bounds array access.
[Mandatory] Attack Surface:
Any application using Capstone to process untrusted X86 code
[Mandatory] Impact Summary:
Denial of Service (DoS)
[Optional] Trigger / Attack vector:
 Disassembling a specially crafted X86 instruction with an ID that triggers the binary search bug.

[Mandatory] Key code/struct excerpt (minimal):
```c
while (first <= last) {
	if (insn_regs_intel_sorted[mid].insn < id) {
		first = mid + 1;
	} else if (insn_regs_intel_sorted[mid].insn == id) {
		if (access) {
			*access = insn_regs_intel_sorted[mid].access;
		}
		return insn_regs_intel_sorted[mid].reg;
	} else {
		if (mid == 0)
			break;
		last = mid - 1;
	}
	mid = (first + last) / 2;
}
```
