[Mandatory] Trigger surface/attack vector:
API call to `X86_insn_reg_intel` with a malicious `id` parameter.

[Mandatory] Exploit primitive(s) available:
out-of-bounds read

[Mandatory] Exploitability summary (1 sentence):
The bug is reliably triggerable by providing a specific `id` value to the function, resulting in an out-of-bounds read that can cause a crash (DoS).

[Mandatory] Exploit script (summary, 3—6 bullets):
- Craft an X86 instruction stream whose internal `id` value will lead to the binary search bug.
- Pass this stream to a vulnerable version of the Capstone engine for disassembly.
- The engine will internally call `X86_insn_reg_intel` with the crafted `id`.
- The miscalculated `mid` index will cause an out-of-bounds read from memory.
- This can lead to a crash of the application using the Capstone engine.

