The Vulnerability
[Optional] CWE/CVE Number and description:
CWE-416 / CVE-2017-14989
[Mandatory] Summary:
The vulnerability exists in the RenderFreetype function in magick/annotate.c where a use-after-free condition occurs due to improper management of glyph resources. The function calls FT_Done_Glyph on glyph.image outside the proper conditional scope, potentially leading to memory corruption when the freed resource is accessed later. This can be triggered during font rendering operations when processing specially crafted inputs.
[Mandatory] Root cause:
FT_Done_Glyph is called on glyph.image outside the conditional block where it was allocated, causing premature resource cleanup.
[Mandatory] Attack Surface:
Image processing library via font rendering
[Mandatory] Impact Summary:
Use-after-free leading to potential memory corruption
[Optional] Trigger / Attack vector:
Font file processing during text annotation
[Mandatory] Key code/struct excerpt (minimal):
```c
  ft_status=FT_Get_Glyph(face->glyph,&glyph.image);
  if (ft_status == 0)
    {
      ft_status=FT_Outline_Get_BBox(&((FT_OutlineGlyph) glyph.image)->
        outline,&bounds);
