[Mandatory] Title: CVE-2017-15020 / CWE-125:
NA

[Optional] Disclosure / Patch Dates:
Initial advisory: 2017-10-05 — Patch release: 2017-09-26

[Optional] Affected products/versions:
binutils-gdb (before commit 1da5c9a)

The Vulnerability
[Optional] CWE/CVE Number and description:
 CWE-125: Out-of-bounds Read
[Mandatory] Summary:
 A buffer over-read vulnerability exists in the `parse_line_table` function within `bfd/dwarf1.c` of binutils-gdb. The issue is triggered when processing a malicious DWARF1 debug section, where the code fails to sufficiently validate that a read operation for a line table entry will remain within the bounds of the allocated buffer. This allows an attacker to read past the end of the `line_section` buffer, potentially leading to an information leak or application crash.
[Mandatory] Root cause:
 Insufficient bounds checking on the `xptr` pointer before reading data from the `line_section` buffer.
[Mandatory] Attack Surface:
Local binary utility processing untrusted files (e.g., objdump)
[Mandatory] Impact Summary:
Information disclosure / Denial of Service
[Optional] Trigger / Attack vector:
 Maliciously crafted binary file with a DWARF1 .line section
[Mandatory] Key code/struct excerpt (minimal):

for (eachLine = 0; eachLine < aUnit->line_count; eachLine++)
	{
	  /* A line number.  */
	  aUnit->linenumber_table[eachLine].linenumber
	    = bfd_get_32 (stash->abfd, (bfd_byte *) xptr);
