Maliciously crafted `nodes.conf` file.

[Mandatory] Exploit primitive(s) available:
Arbitrary write (out-of-bounds write)

[Mandatory] Exploitability summary (1 sentence):
Exploitation requires local access to modify the cluster configuration file, but allows for arbitrary memory writes leading to potential code execution.

[Mandatory] Exploit script (summary, 3—6 bullets):

- Attacker gains ability to modify the `nodes.conf` file.
- Attacker crafts a line in the config with an out-of-bounds hash slot index (e.g., a very large number).
- The `clusterLoadConfig` function parses the file and uses the unchecked value as an array index.
- This results in an out-of-bounds write at an attacker-controlled offset.
- The attacker can leverage this to corrupt memory and potentially achieve code execution.

