[Mandatory] ID:
CVE-2017-16643

[Mandatory] Title: CVE-2017-16643 / CWE-125:
Potential out-of-bound access in HID report parser

[Optional] Disclosure / Patch Dates:
NA

[Optional] Affected products/versions:
NA

The Vulnerability
[Optional] CWE/CVE Number and description:
 Out-of-bounds Read
[Mandatory] Summary:
 The bug exists in the parse_hid_report_descriptor() function where a while loop only checks that there is at least 1 byte remaining (i < length) but the loop body can read multiple bytes from the report buffer. This causes out-of-bounds access when processing specially crafted HID report descriptors.
[Mandatory] Root cause:
 Insufficient bounds checking before reading multiple bytes in the HID report parsing loop.
[Mandatory] Attack Surface:
Input device driver (tablet)
[Mandatory] Impact Summary:
Out-of-bounds read → potential information disclosure or crash
[Optional] Trigger / Attack vector:
 Malformed HID report descriptor
[Mandatory] Key code/struct excerpt (minimal):
while (i < length) {
		prefix = report[i++];
		/* Determine data size and save the data in the proper variable */
		size = (1U << PREF_SIZE(prefix)) >> 1;
		if (i + size > length) {
			dev_err(ddev,
				"Not enough data (need %d, have %d)\n",
				i + size, length);
			break;
		}
		switch (size) {
		case 1:
			data = report[i];
			break;
		case 2:
			data16 = get_unaligned_le16(&report[i]);
			break;
		case 4:
			data32 = get_unaligned_le32(&report[i]);
			break;
		}
		/* Skip size of data */
		i += size;
