[Mandatory] ID:
CVE-2017-13010

[Mandatory] Title: CVE-2017-13010 / CWE-125:
Buffer over-read in BEEP parser

[Optional] Disclosure / Patch Dates:
Initial advisory: 2017-09-14 — Patch release: Not available in input

[Optional] Affected products/versions:
Not available in input

The Vulnerability
[Optional] CWE/CVE Number and description:
CWE-125: Out-of-bounds Read
[Mandatory] Summary:
The vulnerability exists in the `beep_print` function within tcpdump, which processes BEEP protocol packets. The function calls `l_strnstart` without passing the `ndo` (netdissect options) context, leading to insufficient bounds checking when comparing packet data against fixed strings. This allows an attacker to trigger a buffer over-read by crafting a packet with insufficient length, potentially causing a crash or information disclosure.
[Mandatory] Root cause:
Missing bounds checking due to incorrect arguments passed to `l_strnstart`.
[Mandatory] Attack Surface:
Network packet parser (tcpdump)
[Mandatory] Impact Summary:
Denial of service or information disclosure via buffer over-read.
[Optional] Trigger / Attack vector:
Malformed BEEP packet over the network.
[Mandatory] Key code/struct excerpt (minimal):
```c
void
beep_print(netdissect_options *ndo, const u_char *bp, u_int length)
{

	if (l_strnstart(ndo, "MSG", 4, (const char *)bp, length)) /* A REQuest */
		ND_PRINT((ndo, " BEEP MSG"));
