		ND_PRINT((ndo, " BEEP END"));
	else
		ND_PRINT((ndo, " BEEP (payload or undecoded)"));
}
```
[Mandatory] Fix summary:
The fix adds the missing `ndo` argument to all `l_strnstart` calls in `beep_print`, ensuring proper bounds checking is performed before reading packet data.
[Optional] Patch reference:
https://github.com/the-tcpdump-group/tcpdump/commit/877b66b398518d9501513e0860c9f3a8acc70892
