The Vulnerability
[Optional] CWE/CVE Number and description:
CWE-125: Out-of-bounds Read
[Mandatory] Summary:
The vulnerability exists in the `cfm_network_addr_print` function within `print-cfm.c`. The function reads network address types and their corresponding addresses from a packet buffer without sufficient validation of the buffer length. This can lead to an out-of-bounds read when processing crafted packets with insufficient length for the specified address type (IPv4 or IPv6).
[Mandatory] Root cause:
The function lacks proper bounds checks on the input buffer length before dereferencing pointers to read IP address data.
[Mandatory] Attack Surface:
Network packet parser (tcpdump)
[Mandatory] Impact Summary:
Denial of service via application crash
[Optional] Trigger / Attack vector:
Crafted network packet with CFM TLV
[Mandatory] Key code/struct excerpt (minimal):
```c
    case AFNUM_INET:
