[Mandatory] ID:
CVE-2017-13688

[Mandatory] Title: CVE-2017-13688 / CWE-125:
Out-of-bounds Read

[Optional] Disclosure / Patch Dates:
Initial advisory: 2017-09-14 — Patch release: Not available in input

[Optional] Affected products/versions:
Not available in input

The Vulnerability
[Optional] CWE/CVE Number and description:
CWE-125
[Mandatory] Summary:
The vulnerability is an out-of-bounds read in the OLSR packet parser within tcpdump. It is triggered when processing a crafted OLSR packet where the parser reads packet header fields before performing sufficient bounds checks. This allows reading past the end of the supplied packet buffer, potentially leaking memory contents.
[Mandatory] Root cause:
The parser reads data from the packet before verifying that enough bytes remain to satisfy the read operation.
[Mandatory] Attack Surface:
Network packet capture analysis (tcpdump)
[Mandatory] Impact Summary:
Information leak via out-of-bounds read
[Optional] Trigger / Attack vector:
Crafted OLSR packet on the network
[Mandatory] Key code/struct excerpt (minimal):
        ND_TCHECK2(*tptr, sizeof(struct olsr_msg4));

        if (is_ipv6)
        {
            msgptr.v6 = (const struct olsr_msg6 *) tptr;
            msg_type = msgptr.v6->msg_type;
            msg_len = EXTRACT_16BITS(msgptr.v6->msg_len);
