[Mandatory] ID:
CVE-2017-14687

[Mandatory] Title: CVE-2017-14687 / CWE-119:
Handle non-tags in tag name comparisons

[Optional] Disclosure / Patch Dates:
Initial advisory: 2017-09-22 — Patch release: 2017-09-19

[Optional] Affected products/versions:
Not available in input

The Vulnerability
[Optional] CWE/CVE Number and description:
 Improper Restriction of Operations within the Bounds of a Memory Buffer
[Mandatory] Summary:
 The vulnerability exists in the `xps_parse_brush` function within `source/xps/xps-common.c`. The function processes XML nodes to parse different types of brushes. In the original code, when an unknown tag is encountered, the function calls `fz_warn` with the result of `fz_xml_tag(node)`. If `node` is not a valid tag, `fz_xml_tag` could return a pointer that leads to an out-of-bounds memory read, making the bug exploitable.
[Mandatory] Root cause:
 The call to `fz_xml_tag(node)` without verifying that `node` is a valid tag can lead to an out-of-bounds read.
[Mandatory] Attack Surface:
Not available in input
[Mandatory] Impact Summary:
Not available in input
[Optional] Trigger / Attack vector:
Not available in input
[Mandatory] Key code/struct excerpt (minimal):
void
xps_parse_brush(fz_context *ctx, xps_document *doc, const fz_matrix *ctm, const fz_rect *area, char *base_uri, xps_resource *dict, fz_xml *node)
{
	if (doc->cookie && doc->cookie->abort)
		return;
	/* SolidColorBrushes are handled in a special case and will never show up here */
	if (fz_xml_is_tag(node, "ImageBrush"))
		xps_parse_image_brush(ctx, doc, ctm, area, base_uri, dict, node);
	else if (fz_xml_is_tag(node, "VisualBrush"))
		xps_parse_visual_brush(ctx, doc, ctm, area, base_uri, dict, node);
	else if (fz_xml_is_tag(node, "LinearGradientBrush"))
		xps_parse_linear_gradient_brush(ctx, doc, ctm, area, base_uri, dict, node);
	else if (fz_xml_is_tag(node, "RadialGradientBrush"))
		xps_parse_radial_gradient_brush(ctx, doc, ctm, area, base_uri, dict, node);
	else
		fz_warn(ctx, "unknown brush tag: %s", fz_xml_tag(node));
}

