[Mandatory] ID:
CVE-2017-14729

[Mandatory] Title: CVE-2017-14729 / CWE-119:
Memory corruption in PLT processing

[Optional] Disclosure / Patch Dates:
Initial advisory: 2017-09-25 — Patch release: Not available in input

[Optional] Affected products/versions:
Not available in input

The Vulnerability
[Optional] CWE/CVE Number and description:
CWE-119
[Mandatory] Summary:
A vulnerability exists in the `elf_i386_get_synthetic_symtab` function where a corrupted Procedure Linkage Table (PLT) can cause the same relocation entry to be processed multiple times. This occurs because the code does not guard against duplicate PLT entries for a single symbol, leading to improper symbol table generation.
[Mandatory] Root cause:
The code fails to nullify the `howto` pointer of a relocation entry after processing it, allowing subsequent iterations to match and process the same entry again from a corrupted PLT.
[Mandatory] Attack Surface:
Local file parsing (e.g., objdump, ld)
[Mandatory] Impact Summary:
Potential memory corruption or denial of service
[Optional] Trigger / Attack vector:
Malicious ELF binary with crafted PLT entries
[Mandatory] Key code/struct excerpt (minimal):

    /* Skip unknown relocation.  PR 17512: file: bc9d6cf5.  */
    if (got_vma == p->address
		&& p->howto != NULL
		&& (p->howto->type == R_386_JUMP_SLOT
		    || p->howto->type == R_386_GLOB_DAT
		    || p->howto->type == R_386_IRELATIVE))
      {
	*s = **p->sym_ptr_ptr;
	/* Undefined syms won't have BSF_LOCAL or BSF_GLOBAL
	   set.  Since we are defining a symbol, ensure one
	   of them is set.  */
	if ((s->flags & BSF_LOCAL) == 0)
	  s->flags |= BSF_GLOBAL;
	s->flags |= BSF_SYNTHETIC;
	/* This is no longer a section symbol.  */
	s->flags &= ~BSF_SECTION_SYM;
	s->section = plt;
	s->the_bfd = plt->owner;
	s->value = offset;
	/* Store relocation for later use.  */
	s->udata.p = p;
	/* Add @plt to function name later.  */
	size += strlen (s->name) + sizeof ("@plt");
	if (p->addend != 0)
	  size += sizeof ("+0x") - 1 + 8;
	n++;
	s++;
      }

Exploit:

[Mandatory] Trigger surface/attack vector:
Malicious ELF binary processed by binutils tools

[Mandatory] Exploit primitive(s) available:
Not available in input

[Mandatory] Exploitability summary (1 sentence):
The exploitability depends on the ability to craft a corrupted PLT that triggers duplicate processing of relocation entries.

[Mandatory] Exploit script (summary, 3—6 bullets):
- Craft an ELF binary with a PLT section containing duplicate entries.
- Ensure the duplicate entries resolve to the same relocation address.
- Trigger processing with a tool like `objdump -d` or during linking.
- The vulnerability may lead to memory corruption due to repeated processing.

Fix
[Mandatory] Fix code:
    /* Skip unknown relocation.  PR 17512: file: bc9d6cf5.  */
    if (got_vma == p->address
		&& p->howto != NULL
		&& (p->howto->type == R_386_JUMP_SLOT
		    || p->howto->type == R_386_GLOB_DAT
		    || p->howto->type == R_386_IRELATIVE))
      {
	*s = **p->sym_ptr_ptr;
	/* Undefined syms won't have BSF_LOCAL or BSF_GLOBAL
	   set.  Since we are defining a symbol, ensure one
	   of them is set.  */
	if ((s->flags & BSF_LOCAL) == 0)
	  s->flags |= BSF_GLOBAL;
	s->flags |= BSF_SYNTHETIC;
	/* This is no longer a section symbol.  */
	s->flags &= ~BSF_SECTION_SYM;
	s->section = plt;
	s->the_bfd = plt->owner;
	s->value = offset;
	/* Store relocation for later use.  */
	s->udata.p = p;
	/* Add @plt to function name later.  */
	size += strlen (s->name) + sizeof ("@plt");
	if (p->addend != 0)
	  size += sizeof ("+0x") - 1 + 8;
	n++;
	s++;
	/* There should be only one entry in PLT for a given
	   symbol.  Set howto to NULL after processing a PLT
	   entry to guard against corrupted PLT.  */
	p->howto = NULL;
      }

[Mandatory] Fix summary:
The patch adds a nullification of the `howto` pointer after processing a PLT entry to prevent duplicate processing in case of a corrupted PLT.

