[Mandatory] ID:
CVE-2017-14976

[Mandatory] Title: CVE-2017-14976 / CWE-125:
Out-of-bounds read

[Optional] Disclosure / Patch Dates:
Initial advisory: 2017-10-02 — Patch release: Not available in input

[Optional] Affected products/versions:
Not available in input

The Vulnerability
[Optional] CWE/CVE Number and description:
CWE-125: Out-of-bounds read
[Mandatory] Summary:
The bug is in the `FoFiType1C::convertToType0` function where a file descriptor (`fd`) derived from a font data structure is used to index into the `privateDicts` array without validation. If `fd` is greater than or equal to the number of font dictionaries (`nFDs`), the subsequent access to `privateDicts[fd]` results in an out-of-bounds read. This can be triggered by processing a specially crafted font file, leading to potential information disclosure.
[Mandatory] Root cause:
Lack of bounds check on the `fd` index before using it to access the `privateDicts` array.
[Mandatory] Attack Surface:
Font parser (e.g., PDF renderer)
[Mandatory] Impact Summary:
Information disclosure
[Optional] Trigger / Attack vector:
Specially crafted Type 1C font file
[Mandatory] Key code/struct excerpt (minimal):
      // if fdSelect is NULL, we have an 8-bit font, so just leave fd=0
      if (fdSelect) {
	for (j = i==0 ? 1 : 0; j < 256 && i+j < nCIDs; ++j) {
	  if (cidMap[i+j] >= 0) {
	    fd = fdSelect[cidMap[i+j]];
	    break;
	  }
	}
      }

      if (fd >= nFDs)
	continue;

      // font dictionary (unencrypted section)
      (*outputFunc)(outputStream, "16 dict begin\n", 14);
      if (privateDicts[fd].hasFontMatrix) {
	buf = GooString::format("/FontMatrix [{0:.8g} {1:.8g} {2:.8g} {3:.8g} {4:.8g} {5:.8g}] def\n",
				      privateDicts[fd].fontMatrix[0],
				      privateDicts[fd].fontMatrix[1],
				      privateDicts[fd].fontMatrix[2],
				      privateDicts[fd].fontMatrix[3],
				      privateDicts[fd].fontMatrix[4],
				      privateDicts[fd].fontMatrix[5]);
	(*outputFunc)(outputStream, buf->getCString(), buf->getLength());
	delete buf;
      }

Exploit:

[Mandatory] Trigger surface/attack vector:
Font parsing API, specifically when processing a Type1C font.

[Mandatory] Exploit primitive(s) available:
Out-of-bounds read

[Mandatory] Exploitability summary (1 sentence):
The exploit is controlled by the font data, allowing an attacker to read memory past the `privateDicts` array.

[Mandatory] Exploit script (summary, 3—6 bullets):
- Create a malicious Type1C font file.
- Manipulate the font data to cause `fdSelect` to yield a value `fd` >= `nFDs`.
- Trigger the parsing of the font via a vulnerable application.
- The application will read out-of-bounds from `privateDicts[fd]`.
- Potentially leak memory contents.

Fix
[Mandatory] Fix code:
      // if fdSelect is NULL, we have an 8-bit font, so just leave fd=0
      if (fdSelect) {
	for (j = i==0 ? 1 : 0; j < 256 && i+j < nCIDs; ++j) {
	  if (cidMap[i+j] >= 0) {
	    fd = fdSelect[cidMap[i+j]];
	    break;
	  }
	}
      }

      if (fd >= nFDs)
	continue;

[Mandatory] Fix summary:
The patch adds a bounds check to ensure that `fd` is within the valid range of `privateDicts` before any array access. If `fd` is out of bounds, the loop continues to the next iteration, preventing the out-of-bounds read.

[Optional] Patch reference:
Commit da63c35549e8852a410946ab016a3f25ac701bdf
[Optional] Patch Analysis:
What did the fix do?
- Field: PatchType (bounds check added)
[Optional] Variant & Triage Guidance

[Optional] Variant analysis suggestions (2—3 bullets):
- Review other locations in the codebase where `fdSelect` or similar indices are used to access arrays.
- Fuzz Type1C font parsers to find similar missing bounds checks.
- Diff forks of the project to see if they have introduced similar issues.

[Optional] Likely variants/impact (one line):
Other instances of unvalidated array indexing could lead to similar out-of-bounds reads or writes.

