The Vulnerability
[Optional] CWE/CVE Number and description:
CWE-120: Buffer Copy without Checking Size of Input ('Classic Buffer Overflow')
[Mandatory] Summary:
The vulnerability is in the `UnicodeBlockCanvas::RequestBuffers` function, where the size for two reallocations (`new_backing` and `new_empty`) is calculated using only `width` and `height` without accounting for an extra pixel needed when rendering columns of uneven width. This miscalculation leads to an undersized buffer allocation. When the code subsequently writes to this buffer, it can write past the allocated bounds, resulting in a heap-based buffer overflow.
[Mandatory] Root cause:
The buffer size calculation `width * (height + 1) * sizeof(rgba_t)` and `width * sizeof(rgba_t)` does not include the necessary space for overhang pixels in quarter-rendering of uneven columns.
[Mandatory] Attack Surface:
Local application (timg image viewer)
[Mandatory] Impact Summary:
Heap buffer overflow leading to application crash or potential arbitrary code execution.
[Optional] Trigger / Attack vector:
Specially crafted image or terminal dimensions that trigger quarter-rendering with uneven column widths.
[Mandatory] Key code/struct excerpt (minimal):
    const size_t new_backing = width * (height + 1) * sizeof(rgba_t);
    if (new_backing > backing_buffer_size_) {
        backing_buffer_      = (rgba_t *)realloc(backing_buffer_, new_backing);
        backing_buffer_size_ = new_backing;
    }

    const size_t new_empty = width * sizeof(rgba_t);
    if (new_empty > empty_line_size_) {
        empty_line_      = (rgba_t *)realloc(empty_line_, new_empty);
        empty_line_size_ = new_empty;
        memset(empty_line_, 0x00, empty_line_size_);
    }
