files.src/gd_io_dp.c:
static int dynamicGetbuf(gdIOCtxPtr ctx, void *buf, int len)
{
	int rlen, remain;
	dpIOCtxPtr dctx;
	dynamicPtr *dp;

	dctx = (dpIOCtxPtr) ctx;
	dp = dctx->dp;

	if (dp->pos < 0 || dp->pos >= dp->realSize) {
		return 0;
	}

	remain = dp->logicalSize - dp->pos;
	if(remain >= len) {
		rlen = len;
	} else {
		if(remain <= 0) {
			return 0;
		}

		rlen = remain;
	}

	if (dp->pos + rlen > dp->realSize) {
		rlen = dp->realSize - dp->pos;
	}

	memcpy(buf, (void *) ((char *)dp->data + dp->pos), rlen);
	dp->pos += rlen;

	return rlen;
}

annotation:
[Mandatory] ID:
CVE-2016-6911

[Mandatory] Title: CVE-2016-6911 / CWE-125: Invalid read in gdImageCreateFromTiffPtr

[Optional] Disclosure / Patch Dates:
Initial advisory: 2017-01-26 — Patch release: 2016-08-03

[Optional] Affected products/versions:
libgd — versions not available in input

The Vulnerability
[Optional] CWE/CVE Number and description:
 CWE-125 (Invalid read) / CVE-2016-6911
[Mandatory] Summary:
 An invalid read vulnerability exists in the `dynamicGetbuf` function within `src/gd_io_dp.c`. The bug is triggered when processing a specially crafted corrupt TIFF file that causes the function to be called with a negative `dp->pos`. This leads to an out-of-bounds memory read in the `memcpy` call because the initial position check is missing, allowing an attacker to read memory contents adjacent to the intended buffer.
[Mandatory] Root cause:
 Missing validation for an out-of-bounds `dp->pos` field before memory access.
[Mandatory] Attack Surface:
Image processing library (libgd) via a crafted TIFF file.
[Mandatory] Impact Summary:
Information leak / Denial of Service (crash)
[Optional] Trigger / Attack vector:
 A corrupt TIFF file processed by libgd.
[Mandatory] Key code/struct excerpt (minimal):
dctx = (dpIOCtxPtr) ctx;
dp = dctx->dp;

remain = dp->logicalSize - dp->pos;
if(remain >= len) {
	rlen = len;
} else {
	if(remain <= 0) {
		return 0;
	}

	rlen = remain;
}

memcpy(buf, (void *) ((char *)dp->data + dp->pos), rlen);
dp->pos += rlen;

return rlen;
Exploit:

[Mandatory] Trigger surface/attack vector:
A corrupt TIFF file processed by the libgd library.

[Mandatory] Exploit primitive(s) available:
Arbitrary read from memory adjacent to the `dp->data` buffer.

[Mandatory] Exploitability summary (1 sentence):
Exploitability is moderate, requiring a specifically crafted file to trigger the out-of-bounds read, potentially leading to an information leak or application crash.

[Mandatory] Exploit script (summary, 3—6 bullets):
- Attacker creates a corrupt TIFF file that manipulates the internal state of the `dynamicPtr` structure.
- The file is crafted to set the `dp->pos` field to a negative value during processing.
- The victim application processes the malicious TIFF file using a vulnerable version of libgd.
- The processing calls `gdImageCreateFromTiffPtr`, which in turn calls the vulnerable `dynamicGetbuf` function.
- `dynamicGetbuf` uses the negative `dp->pos` in a pointer arithmetic calculation for a `memcpy` operation.
- This results in an out-of-bounds memory read from an address preceding the `dp->data` buffer, leading to a crash or information disclosure.

Fix
[Mandatory] Fix code:
dctx = (dpIOCtxPtr) ctx;
dp = dctx->dp;

if (dp->pos < 0 || dp->pos >= dp->realSize) {
	return 0;
}

remain = dp->logicalSize - dp->pos;
if(remain >= len) {
	rlen = len;
} else {
	if(remain <= 0) {
		return 0;
	}

	rlen = remain;
}
if (dp->pos + rlen > dp->realSize) {
	rlen = dp->realSize - dp->pos;
}

[Mandatory] Fix summary:
 The patch adds a bounds check at the beginning of the `dynamicGetbuf` function to ensure `dp->pos` is within the valid range (`0 <= dp->pos < dp->realSize`) before any memory access is attempted.
[Optional] Patch reference:
 https://github.com/libgd/libgd/commit/4859d69e07504d4b0a4bdf9bcb4d9e3769ca35ae
[Optional] Patch Analysis:
What did the fix do?
- Field: PatchType (bounds check added)
[Optional] Variant & Triage Guidance

[Optional] Variant analysis suggestions (2—3 bullets):
- Review other functions in the `gd_io_dp.c` file and similar I/O context handlers for missing or insufficient bounds checks on position pointers or buffer lengths.
- Audit all callers of `dynamicGetbuf` to ensure they cannot manipulate the `dynamicPtr` context to an invalid state that bypasses the new check.
- Fuzz the libgd library with various image formats (e.g., TIFF, PNG, JPEG) to uncover other potential out-of-bounds read/write vulnerabilities in the parsers.

[Optional] Likely variants/impact (one line):
Similar out-of-bounds reads likely exist in other image parsing or I/O handling functions.

