NA

[Optional] Disclosure / Patch Dates:
Initial advisory: 2018-12-22 — Patch release: 2019-08-19

[Optional] Affected products/versions:
NA

The Vulnerability
[Optional] CWE/CVE Number and description:
 NA
[Mandatory] Summary:
 The vulnerability exists in the `reconstruct_single_channel` function in `libfaad/specrec.c`. It is triggered when processing an audio stream with Parametric Stereo (PS) that changes the number of output channels after the first frame. The code incorrectly handles memory reallocation in this scenario, leading to memory corruption because it unconditionally resets allocation state without first checking if the stream has more than one channel.
[Mandatory] Root cause:
 The root cause is an unguarded memory reallocation routine that resets the decoder's channel allocation state for multi-channel streams when PS is detected.
[Mandatory] Attack Surface:
Audio decoder
[Mandatory] Impact Summary:
Memory corruption
[Optional] Trigger / Attack vector:
 Crafted audio file with Parametric Stereo
[Mandatory] Key code/struct excerpt (minimal):
