The Vulnerability
[Optional] CWE/CVE Number and description:
CWE-787: Out-of-bounds Write

[Mandatory] Summary:
The bug is in the `ok_csv_decode2` function within `ok_csv.c`. It is triggered when processing a specially crafted CSV input that leads to an out-of-bounds write. The vulnerability is exploitable because the code allocates a buffer of size `peek` without checking if `peek` is zero, and then writes data to it, resulting in a heap corruption.

[Mandatory] Root cause:
The code allocates a buffer of size `peek` without checking if `peek` is zero, leading to an out-of-bounds write.

[Mandatory] Attack Surface:
CSV parser

[Mandatory] Impact Summary:
Heap corruption

[Optional] Trigger / Attack vector:
Specially crafted CSV file

[Mandatory] Key code/struct excerpt (minimal):
```c
            case OK_CSV_NONESCAPED_FIELD: {
                if (curr_char == ',' || curr_char == '\r' || curr_char == '\n' || is_eof) {
                    char *field = malloc(peek);
                    if (!field) {
                        ok_csv_error(csv, "Couldn't allocate field");
                        return;
                    }
                    ok_csv_circular_buffer_read(&decoder->input_buffer, (unsigned char *)field,
                                                peek - 1);
                    ok_csv_circular_buffer_skip(&decoder->input_buffer, 1);
                    field[peek - 1] = 0;
                    peek = 0;
```
Exploit:

[Mandatory] Trigger surface/attack vector:
CSV file parsing API

[Mandatory] Exploit primitive(s) available:
Out-of-bounds write

[Mandatory] Exploitability summary (1 sentence):
Controlled input can lead to a predictable out-of-bounds write on the heap.

[Mandatory] Exploit script (summary, 3—6 bullets):
- Create a CSV file that triggers the `OK_CSV_NONESCAPED_FIELD` state with an empty field.
- Ensure the `peek` variable is zero when the allocation occurs.
- The `malloc(peek)` call will allocate a zero-byte buffer.
- The subsequent write to `field[peek - 1]` will be an out-of-bounds write.

Fix
[Mandatory] Fix code:
```c
            case OK_CSV_NONESCAPED_FIELD: {
                if (curr_char == ',' || curr_char == '\r' || curr_char == '\n' || is_eof) {
                    char *field = peek == 0 ? NULL : malloc(peek);
                    if (!field) {
                        ok_csv_error(csv, "Couldn't allocate field");
                        return;
                    }
                    if (peek > 0) {
                        ok_csv_circular_buffer_read(&decoder->input_buffer, (unsigned char *)field,
                                                    peek - 1);
                        ok_csv_circular_buffer_skip(&decoder->input_buffer, 1);
                        field[peek - 1] = 0;
                    }
                    peek = 0;
```

[Mandatory] Fix summary:
The patch adds a check to ensure `peek` is not zero before allocating memory and writing to the buffer, preventing the out-of-bounds write.

