- Review other allocation sites in the parser for similar zero-size allocations.
- Fuzz the CSV parser with inputs that cause various state transitions with minimal field lengths.
- Audit the `ok_csv_ensure_record_capcity` and `ok_csv_ensure_field_capcity` functions for similar issues.

[Optional] Likely variants/impact (one line):
Similar allocation patterns in the parser may lead to other heap corruption vulnerabilities.

