Not available in input

The Vulnerability
[Optional] CWE/CVE Number and description:
CWE-119: Improper Restriction of Operations within the Bounds of a Memory Buffer
[Mandatory] Summary:
The vulnerability exists in the check_user_password function within libclamav/pdf.c. If the R parameter is less than 2, the function incorrectly enters a code path intended for revisions 2 through 4 without proper validation. This leads to an unchecked length field being used in subsequent MD5 hash calculations, potentially resulting in a buffer over-read or over-write when length exceeds the size of the result buffer.
[Mandatory] Root cause:
The else condition for handling R revisions lacks a bounds check, allowing invalid R values to skip length validation.
[Mandatory] Attack Surface:
PDF parser in ClamAV antivirus engine.
[Mandatory] Impact Summary:
Denial of service via memory corruption.
[Optional] Trigger / Attack vector:
Specially crafted PDF file.
