Exploit:

[Mandatory] Trigger surface/attack vector:
File format parser (PDF).

[Mandatory] Exploit primitive(s) available:
Out-of-bounds read/write.

[Mandatory] Exploitability summary (1 sentence):
Controlled input via a crafted PDF file can trigger the memory corruption, potentially leading to a crash.

[Mandatory] Exploit script (summary, 3—6 bullets):
- Craft a PDF file with an R value less than 2 (e.g., 1).
- Set the length field to a value greater than 128.
- Ensure the O and U fields are present to reach the vulnerable code path.
- The length check is bypassed, leading to an out-of-bounds operation on the result buffer.
- The resulting memory corruption can cause the ClamAV scanner to crash.

Fix
[Mandatory] Fix code:
    } else if ((R >= 2) && (R <= 4)) {
	/* 7.6.3.3 Algorithm 2 */
	cli_md5_init(&md5);
	/* empty password, password == padding */
	cli_md5_update(&md5, key_padding, 32);
	cli_md5_update(&md5, O, 32);
	P = le32_to_host(P);
	cli_md5_update(&md5, &P, 4);
	cli_md5_update(&md5, pdf->fileID, pdf->fileIDlen);
	if (R >= 4 && !EM) {
