[Mandatory] ID:
CVE-2011-4098

[Mandatory] Title: CVE-2011-4098 / CWE-119:
GFS2 fallocate memory corruption

[Optional] Disclosure / Patch Dates:
Initial advisory: 2013-06-08 — Patch release: Not available in input

[Optional] Affected products/versions:
Not available in input

The Vulnerability
[Optional] CWE/CVE Number and description:
CWE-119
[Mandatory] Summary:
A memory corruption vulnerability exists in the GFS2 filesystem's `fallocate_chunk` function within `fs/gfs2/file.c`. The function improperly handles block allocation, potentially leading to out-of-bounds memory operations when processing fallocate requests. This flaw can be triggered by a local user issuing a fallocate call on a GFS2 filesystem, which could corrupt kernel memory due to improper handling of buffer metadata.
[Mandatory] Root cause:
Incorrect block mapping and buffer state handling during hole allocation.
[Mandatory] Attack Surface:
Local filesystem operations (fallocate syscall).
[Mandatory] Impact Summary:
Local privilege escalation / Denial of Service
[Optional] Trigger / Attack vector:
fallocate syscall on a GFS2-mounted filesystem.
[Mandatory] Key code/struct excerpt (minimal):
```c
while (len) {
    struct buffer_head bh_map = { .b_state = 0, .b_blocknr = 0 };
    bh_map.b_size = len;
    set_buffer_zeronew(&bh_map);

    error = gfs2_block_map(inode, lblock, &bh_map, 1);
    if (unlikely(error))
