The Vulnerability
[Optional] CWE/CVE Number and description:
 Improper Restriction of Operations within the Bounds of a Memory Buffer
[Mandatory] Summary:
 A memory bounds checking error exists in the gfs2_bmap_alloc function within fs/gfs2/bmap.c. When allocating data blocks for a file, the function writes block numbers into an indirect block without sufficiently validating that the write operation remains within the bounds of the allocated buffer. This can lead to an out-of-bounds write, potentially corrupting adjacent memory.
[Mandatory] Root cause:
 Lack of a bounds check before writing block numbers into an indirect block buffer.
[Mandatory] Attack Surface:
Local filesystem operations
[Mandatory] Impact Summary:
Local privilege escalation
[Optional] Trigger / Attack vector:
Fallocate system call on a GFS2 filesystem
