annotation:
[Mandatory] ID:
CVE-2013-6623

[Mandatory] Title: CVE-2013-6623 / CWE-119:
layout recursion vulnerability

[Optional] Disclosure / Patch Dates:
Initial advisory: 2013-11-13 — Patch release: 2013-09-27

[Optional] Affected products/versions:
Chromium (pre-commit a4e53f62f8a1d500a1950d123600bd47214c06d8)

The Vulnerability
[Optional] CWE/CVE Number and description:
 Improper Restriction of Operations within the Bounds of a Memory Buffer
[Mandatory] Summary:
 A bug exists in the `RenderSVGResourceMarker::layout` function where a re-layout mechanism, `RenderSVGRoot::addResourceForClientInvalidation`, could be called inappropriately, leading to invariant violations. The function lacked a guard to prevent recursive layout calls, which could be triggered during SVG resource dependency handling. This would leave render tree nodes marked for layout at paint time, as described in the commit message.
[Mandatory] Root cause:
 Lack of a guard against recursive layout calls and an incorrect dependency invalidation mechanism.
[Mandatory] Attack Surface:
Browser renderer (SVG processing)
[Mandatory] Impact Summary:
Denial of Service (render tree invariant violation, potential crash)
[Optional] Trigger / Attack vector:
Maliciously crafted SVG document causing resource dependency cycles.
[Mandatory] Key code/struct excerpt (minimal):
```cpp
void RenderSVGResourceMarker::layout()
{
    ASSERT(needsLayout());
    if (m_isInLayout)
        return;

    TemporaryChange<bool> inLayoutChange(m_isInLayout, true);

    // Invalidate all resources if our layout changed.
    if (everHadLayout() && selfNeedsLayout())
        removeAllClientsFromCache();

    // RenderSVGHiddenContainer overwrites layout(). We need the
    // layouting of RenderSVGContainer for calculating  local
    // transformations and repaint.
    RenderSVGContainer::layout();
}
```
Exploit:

[Mandatory] Trigger surface/attack vector:
SVG document processing

[Mandatory] Exploit primitive(s) available:
Recursive layout invocation leading to invariant violation.

[Mandatory] Exploitability summary (1 sentence):
Exploitability is limited to causing a denial-of-service by triggering a layout assertion failure or hang.

[Mandatory] Exploit script (summary, 3—6 bullets):
- Create an SVG document with a marker element.
- Structure the document to trigger a layout of the marker.
- Ensure the layout process invalidates a client that, in turn, invalidates the marker again.
- This causes a recursive layout cycle.
- The process hits an `ASSERT` or hangs, crashing the renderer.

Fix
[Mandatory] Fix code:
```cpp
void RenderSVGResourceMarker::layout()
{
    ASSERT(needsLayout());
    if (m_isInLayout)
        return;

    TemporaryChange<bool> inLayoutChange(m_isInLayout, true);

    // Invalidate all resources if our layout changed.
    if (everHadLayout() && selfNeedsLayout())
        removeAllClientsFromCache();

    // RenderSVGHiddenContainer overwrites layout(). We need the
    // layouting of RenderSVGContainer for calculating  local
    // transformations and repaint.
    RenderSVGContainer::layout();
}
```

[Mandatory] Fix summary:
 The patch adds a guard against recursive layout calls using the `m_isInLayout` flag and changes the invalidation logic from `RenderSVGRoot::addResourceForClientInvalidation` to `removeAllClientsFromCache` to break the cycle.

[Optional] Patch reference:
 Commit a4e53f62f8a1d500a1950d123600bd47214c06d8
[Optional] Patch Analysis:
 What did the fix do?
- Field: PatchType (bounds check added, logic refactor, feature removal)
[Optional] Variant & Triage Guidance

[Optional] Variant analysis suggestions (2—3 bullets):
- Review other `RenderSVGResource` subclasses for similar missing recursion guards.
- Fuzz SVG documents with complex resource dependency graphs.
- Diff forks of Blink/WebKit for similar re-layout logic.

[Optional] Likely variants/impact (one line):
Similar recursion bugs could exist in other SVG resource layout handlers.

