The bug is in the `ReadResponseHeaders` function of `net/http/http_stream_parser.cc`. When handling buffered data, the code incorrectly calculates the result size and sets the buffer offset using `read_buf_unused_offset_`, which can lead to processing stale or out-of-bounds data. This is exploitable because an attacker can influence the network stream to trigger this state, causing memory corruption.
