[Mandatory] ID:
CVE-2013-0874

[Mandatory] Title: CVE-2013-0874 / CWE-119:
Buffer overflow in shorts2str

[Optional] Disclosure / Patch Dates:
Initial advisory: 2013-11-23 — Patch release: Not available in input

[Optional] Affected products/versions:
ffmpeg (pre-2013-02-13 commit e1219cdaf9fb4bc8cea410e1caf802373c1bfe51)

The Vulnerability
[Optional] CWE/CVE Number and description:
CWE-119
[Mandatory] Summary:
The vulnerability exists in the `shorts2str` function in `libavcodec/tiff.c`. It is triggered when the function processes a large number of elements, leading to an integer overflow during the calculation of the buffer size to allocate. This results in an undersized buffer being allocated, which is then overflowed by the `snprintf` loop, making the bug exploitable.
[Mandatory] Root cause:
Unchecked integer overflow in the buffer size calculation.
[Mandatory] Attack Surface:
Media parser (TIFF decoder)
[Mandatory] Impact Summary:
Arbitrary code execution via crafted media file.
[Optional] Trigger / Attack vector:
Malicious TIFF file processed by libavcodec.
[Mandatory] Key code/struct excerpt (minimal):
```c
    component_len = 7LL + strlen(sep);
    if (count >= (INT_MAX - 1)/component_len)
        return NULL;
    ap = av_malloc(component_len * count + 1);
