[Mandatory] ID:
CVE-2013-4263

[Mandatory] Title: CVE-2013-4263 / CWE-119:
Out of array accesses

[Optional] Disclosure / Patch Dates:
Initial advisory: 2013-11-23 — Patch release: Not available in input

[Optional] Affected products/versions:
FFmpeg (pre-e43a0a232dbf6d3c161823c2e07c52e76227a1bc)

The Vulnerability
[Optional] CWE/CVE Number and description:
CWE-119: Improper Restriction of Operations within the Bounds of a Memory Buffer

[Mandatory] Summary:
The vulnerability exists in the `filter_frame` function within `libavfilter/vf_lut.c`. When processing planar video data, the loop condition `for (plane = 0; plane < 4 && in->data[plane]; plane++)` checks for the presence of a data plane but fails to validate the associated `linesize[plane]`. This omission allows the loop to process planes with a data pointer but a zero or invalid linesize, leading to out-of-bounds memory reads and writes when the loop attempts to iterate using the linesize stride.

[Mandatory] Root cause:
The for loop condition checks `in->data[plane]` but omits a check for `in->linesize[plane]`, allowing invalid linesizes to be used.

[Mandatory] Attack Surface:
Video filter processing in FFmpeg.

[Mandatory] Impact Summary:
Out-of-bounds memory access, potentially leading to information disclosure or denial of service.

[Optional] Trigger / Attack vector:
A crafted video file that triggers the lut filter with a frame containing a plane where the data pointer is non-NULL but the linesize is zero.

[Mandatory] Key code/struct excerpt (minimal):
```c
        /* planar */
        for (plane = 0; plane < 4 && in->data[plane]; plane++) {
            int vsub = plane == 1 || plane == 2 ? s->vsub : 0;
            int hsub = plane == 1 || plane == 2 ? s->hsub : 0;
            int h = FF_CEIL_RSHIFT(inlink->h, vsub);
            int w = FF_CEIL_RSHIFT(inlink->w, hsub);

