	iob = qeth_get_adapter_cmd(card, IPA_SETADP_SET_SNMP_CONTROL,
					   QETH_SNMP_SETADP_CMDLENGTH + req_len);
	cmd = (struct qeth_ipa_cmd *)(iob->data+IPA_PDU_HEADER_SIZE);
	memcpy(&cmd->data.setadapterparms.data.snmp, &ureq->cmd, req_len);
Exploit:

[Mandatory] Trigger surface/attack vector:
IOCTL

[Mandatory] Exploit primitive(s) available:
Kernel heap buffer overflow

[Mandatory] Exploitability summary (1 sentence):
The exploit is controlled by an attacker-provided length value, enabling a predictable out-of-bounds write in kernel memory.

[Mandatory] Exploit script (summary, 3—6 bullets):
- Attacker issues a malicious IOCTL to the qeth driver.
- The IOCTL payload includes a large `req_len` value.
- `qeth_snmp_command` copies this length from user space.
- The function allocates memory and copies data based on the oversized length.
- A `memcpy` operation writes past the bounds of a kernel buffer, causing overflow.

Fix
[Mandatory] Fix code:
