[Mandatory] ID:
CVE-2013-0845

[Mandatory] Title: CVE-2013-0845 / CWE-119:
Buffer overflow in alsdec

[Optional] Disclosure / Patch Dates:
Initial advisory: 2013-12-07 — Patch release: Not available in input

[Optional] Affected products/versions:
Not available in input

The Vulnerability
[Optional] CWE/CVE Number and description:
Improper Restriction of Operations within the Bounds of a Memory Buffer
[Mandatory] Summary:
The vulnerability exists in the `read_const_block_data` function within `libavcodec/alsdec.c`. The function did not validate the `block_length` field of the `ALSBlockData` structure before using it, which could lead to writing past the end of a buffer. This is exploitable by processing a specially crafted media file that triggers this code path.
[Mandatory] Root cause:
Missing validation for the `block_length` field before processing block data.
[Mandatory] Attack Surface:
Media decoder (alsdec)
[Mandatory] Impact Summary:
Memory corruption → Potential Remote Code Execution
[Optional] Trigger / Attack vector:
Malformed ALS media file
[Mandatory] Key code/struct excerpt (minimal):
static int read_const_block_data(ALSDecContext *ctx, ALSBlockData *bd)
{
    ALSSpecificConfig *sconf = &ctx->sconf;
    AVCodecContext *avctx    = ctx->avctx;
