[Mandatory] ID:
CVE-2013-7020

[Mandatory] Title: CVE-2013-7020 / CWE-119:
Improper Input Validation

[Optional] Disclosure / Patch Dates:
Initial advisory: [Not available in input] — Patch release: [Not available in input]

[Optional] Affected products/versions:
[Not available in input]

The Vulnerability
[Optional] CWE/CVE Number and description:
Improper Restriction of Operations within the Bounds of a Memory Buffer
[Mandatory] Summary:
The vulnerability is in the `read_header` function within `libavcodec/ffv1dec.c`. When parsing version 0 or 1 headers, the function directly writes values extracted from a bitstream into the `f->colorspace` and `f->avctx->bits_per_raw_sample` fields without first validating them against previously stored values. This behavior can be triggered by processing a specially crafted FFV1 video file and is exploitable because it allows an attacker to change critical decoding parameters mid-stream, potentially leading to memory corruption.
[Mandatory] Root cause:
The function assigns bitstream-derived values to global parameters before performing a consistency check, allowing a state change that bypasses validation.
[Mandatory] Attack Surface:
Multimedia parser (video file decoder)
[Mandatory] Impact Summary:
Memory corruption → Potential Remote Code Execution
[Optional] Trigger / Attack vector:
Specially crafted FFV1 video file
[Mandatory] Key code/struct excerpt (minimal):
```c
        f->colorspace = get_symbol(c, state, 0); //YUV cs type

        if (f->version > 0)
            f->avctx->bits_per_raw_sample = get_symbol(c, state, 0);

        chroma_planes  = get_rac(c, state);
        chroma_h_shift = get_symbol(c, state, 0);
        chroma_v_shift = get_symbol(c, state, 0);
        transparency   = get_rac(c, state);

        if (f->plane_count) {
            if (   chroma_planes != f->chroma_planes
                || chroma_h_shift!= f->chroma_h_shift
                || chroma_v_shift!= f->chroma_v_shift
                || transparency  != f->transparency) {
                av_log(f->avctx, AV_LOG_ERROR, "Invalid change of global parameters\n");
                return AVERROR_INVALIDDATA;
            }
        }
```
Exploit:

[Mandatory] Trigger surface/attack vector:
File format parser (FFV1 video header)

[Mandatory] Exploit primitive(s) available:
Control of decoder state parameters

[Mandatory] Exploitability summary (1 sentence):
The exploit is easily triggered by any user who can supply a malicious video file to the vulnerable decoder, with no special privileges required.

[Mandatory] Exploit script (summary, 3—6 bullets):
- Craft an FFV1 video file where the first header sets initial parameters.
- Include a second header that modifies the `colorspace` and `bits_per_raw_sample` values.
- Ensure `f->plane_count` is non-zero to enter the validation block.
- The modified parameters bypass the incomplete check, corrupting the decoder's state.
- This can lead to misuse of memory allocations later in the decoding process, causing a crash or arbitrary code execution.

Fix
[Mandatory] Fix code:
```c
        int chroma_planes, chroma_h_shift, chroma_v_shift, transparency, colorspace, bits_per_raw_sample;
        unsigned v= get_symbol(c, state, 0);
        if (v >= 2) {
            av_log(f->avctx, AV_LOG_ERROR, "invalid version %d in ver01 header\n", v);
            return AVERROR_INVALIDDATA;
        }
        f->version = v;
        f->ac      = f->avctx->coder_type = get_symbol(c, state, 0);
        if (f->ac > 1) {
            for (i = 1; i < 256; i++)
                f->state_transition[i] = get_symbol(c, state, 1) + c->one_state[i];
        }

        colorspace     = get_symbol(c, state, 0); //YUV cs type
        bits_per_raw_sample = f->version > 0 ? get_symbol(c, state, 0) : f->avctx->bits_per_raw_sample;
        chroma_planes  = get_rac(c, state);
        chroma_h_shift = get_symbol(c, state, 0);
        chroma_v_shift = get_symbol(c, state, 0);
        transparency   = get_rac(c, state);

        if (f->plane_count) {
            if (   colorspace    != f->colorspace
                || bits_per_raw_sample != f->avctx->bits_per_raw_sample
                || chroma_planes != f->chroma_planes
                || chroma_h_shift!= f->chroma_h_shift
                || chroma_v_shift!= f->chroma_v_shift
                || transparency  != f->transparency) {
                av_log(f->avctx, AV_LOG_ERROR, "Invalid change of global parameters\n");
                return AVERROR_INVALIDDATA;
            }
        }

        f->colorspace     = colorspace;
        f->avctx->bits_per_raw_sample = bits_per_raw_sample;
```
[Mandatory] Fix summary:
The patch first stores the incoming `colorspace` and `bits_per_raw_sample` values into local variables. It then includes these local variables in the global parameter consistency check. Only if the check passes does it assign the new values to the FFV1 context, preventing an invalid state change.

[Optional] Patch reference:
Commit b05cd1ea7e45a836f7f6071a716c38bb30326e0f
[Optional] Patch Analysis:
What did the fix do?
- Field: PatchType (bounds check added, logic refactor, feature removal)
[Optional] Variant & Triage Guidance

[Optional] Variant analysis suggestions (2—3 bullets):
- Review other FFV1 header parsing functions for similar patterns of direct assignment before validation.
- Fuzz the FFV1 decoder with headers that change other parameters mid-stream to identify similar logic flaws.
- Audit other multimedia codecs in the codebase for TOCTOU (Time-of-Check-Time-of-Use) issues in header parsing.

[Optional] Likely variants/impact (one line):
Similar validation logic gaps could exist in other codec parsers, leading to comparable memory corruption vulnerabilities.

