The Vulnerability
[Optional] CWE/CVE Number and description:
CWE-119
[Mandatory] Summary:
The bug is in the ff_combine_frame function in libavcodec/parser.c. When av_fast_realloc fails to allocate memory, the function returns an error but does not reset the parser context indexes, leaving them in an inconsistent state. This can be triggered by processing a crafted media stream that forces a memory allocation failure, potentially leading to a heap buffer overflow or information leak in subsequent operations.
[Mandatory] Root cause:
Failure to reset parser context indexes on memory reallocation failure.
[Mandatory] Attack Surface:
Media parser (libavcodec)
[Mandatory] Impact Summary:
Heap buffer overflow → Potential RCE or information leak
[Optional] Trigger / Attack vector:
Crafted media file/stream
[Mandatory] Key code/struct excerpt (minimal):

