Exploit:

[Mandatory] Trigger surface/attack vector:
Media file parsing via libavcodec

[Mandatory] Exploit primitive(s) available:
Out-of-bounds read/write due to stale index values

[Mandatory] Exploitability summary (1 sentence):
Controlled input can trigger allocation failures, leading to exploitable state corruption.

[Mandatory] Exploit script (summary, 3—6 bullets):
- Craft a media file that forces av_fast_realloc to fail.
- Trigger ff_combine_frame parsing of the crafted file.
- On allocation failure, parser indexes are left in a stale state.
- Subsequent operations use these stale indexes, causing OOB access.
- This can lead to heap corruption or information disclosure.

Fix
[Mandatory] Fix code:
        if(!new_buffer) {
            pc->index = 0;
            return AVERROR(ENOMEM);
        }
        pc->buffer = new_buffer;
        memcpy(&pc->buffer[pc->index], *buf, *buf_size);
        pc->index += *buf_size;
        return -1;
    }

    *buf_size=
