    /* append to buffer */
    if(pc->index){
        void* new_buffer = av_fast_realloc(pc->buffer, &pc->buffer_size, next + pc->index + FF_INPUT_BUFFER_PADDING_SIZE);
        if(!new_buffer) {
            pc->overread_index =
            pc->index = 0;
            return AVERROR(ENOMEM);
        }

[Mandatory] Fix summary:
The patch adds explicit resets of pc->index and pc->overread_index to 0 in both error paths where av_fast_realloc fails, ensuring the parser context is left in a consistent state.

[Optional] Patch reference:
https://github.com/FFmpeg/FFmpeg/commit/f31011e9abfb2ae75bb32bc44e2c34194c8dc40a
[Optional] Patch Analysis:
What did the fix do?
- Field: PatchType (bounds check added, logic refactor, feature removal)
[Optional] Variant & Triage Guidance

[Optional] Variant analysis suggestions (2—3 bullets):
- Review other functions in libavcodec that use av_fast_realloc for similar error handling patterns.
- Fuzz media parsers with allocation failure injection to uncover similar state inconsistency bugs.
- Audit all parser context state resets on error paths throughout the codebase.

[Optional] Likely variants/impact (one line):
Similar memory allocation failure handling bugs may exist in other parsers.

