[Mandatory] Title: CVE-2013-6836 / CWE-119:
Memory corruption in ms_escher_get_data

[Optional] Disclosure / Patch Dates:
Initial advisory: 2013-12-19 — Patch release: Not available in input

[Optional] Affected products/versions:
GNOME gnumeric (pre-commit b5480b69345b3c6d56ee0ed9c9e9880bb2a08cdc)

The Vulnerability
[Optional] CWE/CVE Number and description:
CWE-119
[Mandatory] Summary:
The vulnerability exists in the ms_escher_get_data function within plugins/excel/ms-escher.c. When extracting data that spans multiple BIFF records, the function allocates a buffer but fails to properly enforce bounds checks during the merging loop. An attacker can trigger this flaw by providing a crafted Excel file, leading to a buffer overflow and potentially corrupting memory.
[Mandatory] Root cause:
Improper bounds checking on the length of data copied into a dynamically allocated buffer during a record merge operation.
[Mandatory] Attack Surface:
File parser (Excel files)
[Mandatory] Impact Summary:
Denial of Service
[Optional] Trigger / Attack vector:
Maliciously crafted Excel file
[Mandatory] Key code/struct excerpt (minimal):
