Exploit:

[Mandatory] Trigger surface/attack vector:
File format (Excel)

[Mandatory] Exploit primitive(s) available:
Buffer overflow write

[Mandatory] Exploitability summary (1 sentence):
The exploit is controlled by the contents of an Excel file, requiring a user to open the malicious file.

[Mandatory] Exploit script (summary, 3—6 bullets):
- Create a crafted Excel file with specific BIFF record structures.
- Ensure a data request spans multiple records to trigger the merge logic.
- Manipulate record lengths to cause the merge loop to write past the allocated buffer.
- The application will crash when memcpy writes out of bounds.
- This may lead to information disclosure or denial of service.

Fix
[Mandatory] Fix code:
