			...
			if (q->opcode != BIFF_MS_O_DRAWING &&
			    q->opcode != BIFF_MS_O_DRAWING_GROUP &&
			    q->opcode != BIFF_MS_O_DRAWING_SELECTION &&
			    q->opcode != BIFF_CHART_gelframe &&
			    q->opcode != BIFF_CONTINUE) {
				g_warning ("Unexpected record type 0x%x @ 0x%lx;", q->opcode, (long)q->streamPos);
				g_free (buffer);
				return NULL;
			}

[Mandatory] Fix summary:
The fix adds a bounds check before each memcpy operation to prevent writing beyond the allocated buffer and ensures the buffer is freed on error paths.

[Optional] Patch reference:
Commit b5480b69345b3c6d56ee0ed9c9e9880bb2a08cdc
[Optional] Patch Analysis:
What did the fix do?
- Field: PatchType (bounds check added, memory leak fix)
[Optional] Variant & Triage Guidance

[Optional] Variant analysis suggestions (2—3 bullets):
- Review other functions in the BIFF record parsing module for similar merging logic.
- Fuzz the Excel parser with a focus on multi-record data requests.
- Audit all g_malloc'd buffers for proper cleanup on all error exit paths.

[Optional] Likely variants/impact (one line):
Other merge operations in the parser may have similar bounds-checking issues.

