The Vulnerability
[Optional] CWE/CVE Number and description:
CWE-119: Improper Restriction of Operations within the Bounds of a Memory Buffer (Buffer Overflow)
[Mandatory] Summary:
The bug resides in the `xps_parse_color` function within `xps-common.c`. When parsing a `ContextColor` string from an XPS file, the function calculates the number of color components (`n`) and uses this value to loop and write data into a fixed-size `samples` array on the stack. The code fails to validate that `n` does not exceed the size of the `samples` array (`FZ_MAX_COLORS`), leading to a stack buffer overflow. This is triggered by processing a malicious XPS file containing a `ContextColor` string with more components than `FZ_MAX_COLORS`.
[Mandatory] Root cause:
Unchecked number of color components (`n`) from a `ContextColor` string before writing into a fixed-size stack buffer.
