The Vulnerability
[Optional] CWE/CVE Number and description:
 Improper Restriction of Operations within the Bounds of a Memory Buffer
[Mandatory] Summary:
 The vulnerability exists in the `xps_parse_gradient_stops` function where a fixed-size stack buffer `sample[8]` is used to store color data. The function calls `xps_parse_color`, which can write up to `FZ_MAX_COLORS` values into this buffer. If `FZ_MAX_COLORS` is greater than 8, this operation will overflow the bounds of the `sample` array, corrupting the stack.
[Mandatory] Root cause:
 The `sample` stack buffer is declared with a fixed size of 8, while the callee function `xps_parse_color` can write more elements, leading to a buffer overflow.
