The Vulnerability
[Optional] CWE/CVE Number and description:
Improper Restriction of Operations within the Bounds of a Memory Buffer (CWE-119)
[Mandatory] Summary:
A buffer overflow vulnerability exists in the `xc_dom_probe_zimage32_kernel` function within the Xen project's ARM zImage loader. The function reads an end address from the kernel image and uses it to calculate the size of an appended Device Tree Blob (DTB) without sufficient validation. An attacker who can control the kernel image can manipulate the `end` field and the DTB header fields, leading to an out-of-bounds memory write when `dom->kernel_size` is updated with the untrusted `end` value.
[Mandatory] Root cause:
Untrusted data from a kernel image (`zimage[ZIMAGE32_END_OFFSET/4]` and a DTB header) is used to calculate a size and pointer without proper bounds checking, leading to a buffer overflow.
[Mandatory] Attack Surface:
Local privileged context (e.g., a toolstack or management process loading a guest kernel)
[Mandatory] Impact Summary:
Local Privilege Escalation
[Optional] Trigger / Attack vector:
A maliciously crafted ARM32 zImage kernel file supplied to the Xen toolstack.
