[Mandatory] Title: CVE-2020-16300 / CWE-787: Out-of-bounds Write

[Optional] Disclosure / Patch Dates:
Initial advisory: 2020-08-13 — Patch release: Not available in input

[Optional] Affected products/versions:
Not available in input

The Vulnerability
[Optional] CWE/CVE Number and description:
 Out-of-bounds Write
[Mandatory] Summary:
 The vulnerability exists in the `tiff12_print_page` function within `devices/gdevtfnx.c`. When processing page data for a TIFF file, a buffer is allocated based on the raster size (`size`) without accounting for the loop's stride, which reads 6 bytes at a time. If `size` is not a multiple of 6, the loop accesses `src[5]` beyond the allocated buffer, leading to an out-of-bounds write.
[Mandatory] Root cause:
 The allocated buffer size is not large enough to handle the loop's read stride of 6 bytes when the raster size is not a multiple of 6.
[Mandatory] Attack Surface:
Local file processing (TIFF device)
[Mandatory] Impact Summary:
Denial of Service
[Optional] Trigger / Attack vector:
 Malicious file processed by the tiff12nc device
