[Mandatory] ID:
CVE-2020-16301

[Mandatory] Title: CVE-2020-16301 / CWE-120:
Buffer copy without checking size of input

[Optional] Disclosure / Patch Dates:
Initial advisory: [2020-08-13] — Patch release: Not available in input

[Optional] Affected products/versions:
ArtifexSoftware/ghostpdl (pre-commit f54414c8b15b2c27d1dcadd92cfe84f6d15f18dc)

The Vulnerability
[Optional] CWE/CVE Number and description:
CWE-120: Buffer Copy without Checking Size of Input ('Classic Buffer Overflow')
[Mandatory] Summary:
The vulnerability exists in the okiibm_print_page1 function where x_dpi derived from the device is used as an index into the graphics_modes_9 array without sufficient bounds checking. An attacker can trigger this by providing a high DPI value, causing an out-of-bounds read on the graphics_modes_9 array, which can lead to a denial of service.
[Mandatory] Root cause:
The root cause is the use of an unsanitized x_dpi value as an array index without validating that the calculated index is within the bounds of the graphics_modes_9 array.
[Mandatory] Attack Surface:
Printer processing subsystem (via crafted file or print job)
[Mandatory] Impact Summary:
Denial of Service
[Optional] Trigger / Attack vector:
A crafted file or command that sets a high x_dpi value on the device.
[Mandatory] Key code/struct excerpt (minimal):
        static const char graphics_modes_9[5] =
        {
        -1, 0 /*60*/, 1 /*120*/, -1, 3 /*240*/
        };
        ...
        x_dpi = pdev->x_pixels_per_inch;
        if (x_dpi / 60 >= sizeof(graphics_modes_9)/sizeof(graphics_modes_9[0])) {
            return_error(gs_error_rangecheck);
        }
        start_graphics = graphics_modes_9[x_dpi / 60];

Exploit:

[Mandatory] Trigger surface/attack vector:
Printer job processing API (e.g., gs command-line tool)
[Mandatory] Exploit primitive(s) available:
Out-of-bounds read
[Mandatory] Exploitability summary (1 sentence):
The exploit is easy to trigger by setting a high DPI value, leading to a predictable crash.
[Mandatory] Exploit script (summary, 3—6 bullets):
- Craft a document or command that sets the device's x_pixels_per_inch to a value >= 300.
- Invoke the Ghostscript interpreter with the okiibm device and the crafted input.
- The x_dpi / 60 calculation results in an index of 5 or more.
- The code accesses graphics_modes_9 out-of-bounds.
- This causes an AddressSanitizer error and application termination.

Fix
[Mandatory] Fix code:
        x_dpi = pdev->x_pixels_per_inch;
        if (x_dpi / 60 >= sizeof(graphics_modes_9)/sizeof(graphics_modes_9[0])) {
            return_error(gs_error_rangecheck);
