        in_size = line_size * (8 * in_y_mult);
        buf1 = (byte *)gs_malloc(pdev->memory, in_size, 1, "okiibm_print_page(buf1)");
        buf2 = (byte *)gs_malloc(pdev->memory, in_size, 1, "okiibm_print_page(buf2)");
        in = buf1;
        out = buf2;
        out_y_mult = 1;
        start_graphics = graphics_modes_9[x_dpi / 60];
        first_pass = (start_graphics == 3 ? 1 : 0);
        last_pass = first_pass * 2;
        y_passes = (y_9pin_high ? 2 : 1);
        y_step = 0;

[Mandatory] Fix summary:
The fix adds an explicit check to ensure the index derived from x_dpi is within the bounds of the graphics_modes_9 array before it is used, returning an error if it is not.
[Optional] Patch reference:
Commit f54414c8b15b2c27d1dcadd92cfe84f6d15f18dc
[Optional] Patch Analysis:
- What did the fix do?
- Field: PatchType (bounds check added)

[Optional] Variant & Triage Guidance

[Optional] Variant analysis suggestions (2—3 bullets):
- Review other device drivers that use DPI or other device parameters as array indices.
- Fuzz the interpreter with various device settings to uncover similar missing bounds checks.
- Audit other functions within the okiibm driver for similar patterns.

[Optional] Likely variants/impact (one line):
Other device drivers may have similar out-of-bounds reads from device parameters.

