[Mandatory] ID:
CVE-2020-16303

[Mandatory] Title: CVE-2020-16303 / CWE-416:
Use After Free

[Optional] Disclosure / Patch Dates:
Initial advisory: 2020-08-13 — Patch release: Not available in input

[Optional] Affected products/versions:
ArtifexSoftware/ghostpdl (commit 94d8955cb77)

The Vulnerability
[Optional] CWE/CVE Number and description:
CWE-416: Use After Free
[Mandatory] Summary:
The vulnerability is in the `xps_image_end_image` function within `devices/vector/gdevxps.c`. During error handling, a Postscript 'restore' operation could free the image enumerator (`pie`) while the XPS device still held a reference to it. This creates a use-after-free condition if the device subsequently accesses the freed enumerator, as the original function lacked a finalization method to safely clean up resources before the enumerator is freed by the restore operation.
[Mandatory] Root cause:
The image enumerator is freed by a Postscript 'restore' operation while the XPS device still holds a reference to it, leading to a use-after-free.
[Mandatory] Attack Surface:
Postscript/PDF interpreter
[Mandatory] Impact Summary:
Use-after-free leading to potential code execution
[Optional] Trigger / Attack vector:
A crafted Postscript/PDF file that triggers an error after `xps_begin_image` but before `xps_image_end_image`, which then invokes a 'restore'.
[Mandatory] Key code/struct excerpt (minimal):
static int
xps_image_end_image(gx_image_enum_common_t * info, bool draw_last)
{
    xps_image_enum_t *pie = (xps_image_enum_t *)info;
    int code = 0;

    /* N.B. Write the final strip, if any. */

    code = TIFFWriteDirectory(pie->tif);
    TIFFCleanup(pie->tif);

    /* Stuff the image into the zip archive and close the file */
    code = xps_add_tiff_image(pie);
    if (code < 0)
        goto exit;

    /* Reset the brush type to solid */
    xps_setstrokebrush((gx_device_xps *) (pie->dev), xps_solidbrush);
    xps_setfillbrush((gx_device_xps *) (pie->dev), xps_solidbrush);

    /* Add the image relationship */
    code = xps_add_image_relationship(pie);

exit:
    return code;
}
Exploit:

[Mandatory] Trigger surface/attack vector:
Postscript/PDF file processing
[Mandatory] Exploit primitive(s) available:
Use-after-free
[Mandatory] Exploitability summary (1 sentence):
An attacker can control the trigger via a crafted file, but exploitability depends on successfully manipulating the freed object's state.
[Mandatory] Exploit script (summary, 3—6 bullets):
- Create a Postscript/PDF file that initiates an image operation.
- Trigger an error after `xps_begin_image` but before `xps_image_end_image`.
- Ensure the error handler invokes a 'restore' operation.
- The 'restore' frees the image enumerator while the device still holds a reference.
- Subsequent access by the device to the freed enumerator results in a use-after-free.

Fix
[Mandatory] Fix code:
exit:
    if (pie->pcs != NULL)
        rc_decrement(pie->pcs, "xps_image_end_image (pcs)");
    if (pie->buffer != NULL)
        gs_free_object(pie->memory, pie->buffer, "xps_image_end_image");
    if (pie->devc_buffer != NULL)
        gs_free_object(pie->memory, pie->devc_buffer, "xps_image_end_image");

    /* ICC clean up */
