    return code;
[Mandatory] Fix summary:
The patch adds cleanup code to the `exit` block of `xps_image_end_image` to properly free resources and release references held by the image enumerator, preventing a use-after-free when the enumerator is freed by a 'restore' operation.
[Optional] Patch reference:
https://github.com/ArtifexSoftware/ghostpdl/commit/94d8955cb7725eb5f3557ddc02310c76124fdd1a
[Optional] Patch Analysis:
What did the fix do?
- Field: PatchType (bounds check added, logic refactor, feature removal)
The fix is a logic refactor that introduces a finalization routine. It adds explicit cleanup of enumerator resources (pcs, buffer, devc_buffer, icc_link) at the function's exit point to ensure they are released before the enumerator itself can be freed by an external operation like 'restore'.
[Optional] Variant & Triage Guidance

[Optional] Variant analysis suggestions (2—3 bullets):
- Review other image enumerator implementations in Ghostscript for similar patterns where resources are held across save/restore boundaries.
- Fuzz the Postscript/PDF interpreter, focusing on sequences that trigger errors and 'restore' operations within image handling code paths.
- Analyze other device-specific enumerators to ensure they have robust finalization methods to handle premature deallocation.

[Optional] Likely variants/impact (one line):
Similar use-after-free issues may exist in other device enumerator components lacking proper finalization.

