[Mandatory] ID:
CVE-2020-17498

[Mandatory] Title: CVE-2020-17498 / CWE-415:
Double Free

[Optional] Disclosure / Patch Dates:
Initial advisory: 2020-08-13 — Patch release: Not available in input

[Optional] Affected products/versions:
Wireshark (pre-commit 76afda963de4f0b9be24f2d8e873990a5cbf221b)

The Vulnerability
[Optional] CWE/CVE Number and description:
Double Free
[Mandatory] Summary:
The vulnerability exists in the `decompress_lz4` function in `epan/dissectors/packet-kafka.c`. A composite tvbuff (`composite_tvb`) is created unconditionally at function start. If an error occurs before any data is appended, `tvb_composite_finalize` is called on an empty composite, and later, if the function fails, a manual free (`tvb_free_chain`) may be attempted on a tvb already managed by the epan library, leading to a double-free. This is triggered during the dissection of a crafted Kafka packet containing LZ4-compressed data.
[Mandatory] Root cause:
Improper lifecycle management of the composite tvbuff, leading to a potential double-free.
[Mandatory] Attack Surface:
Network packet dissector (Kafka protocol parser)
[Mandatory] Impact Summary:
Denial of Service (via application crash)
[Optional] Trigger / Attack vector:
Malformed Kafka packet with LZ4 compression
[Mandatory] Key code/struct excerpt (minimal):

```c
    tvbuff_t *composite_tvb = tvb_new_composite();
    ...
end:
    if (composite_tvb) {
        tvb_composite_finalize(composite_tvb);
    }
    LZ4F_freeDecompressionContext(lz4_ctxt);
    if (composite_tvb != NULL) {
        tvb_free_chain(composite_tvb);
    }
```

Exploit:

[Mandatory] Trigger surface/attack vector:
Network packet, specifically a Kafka packet with an LZ4 payload.

[Mandatory] Exploit primitive(s) available:
Denial of Service (crash)

[Mandatory] Exploitability summary (1 sentence):
An attacker can trigger the vulnerability by sending a specially crafted packet that causes an error path in the LZ4 decompression routine, leading to a double-free and application crash.

[Mandatory] Exploit script (summary, 3—6 bullets):
- Craft a Kafka packet with an LZ4-compressed payload.
- Ensure the payload triggers an error condition in `decompress_lz4` before any data is appended to `composite_tvb`.
- Send the packet to a target system running a vulnerable version of Wireshark.
- The dissector will enter the error cleanup path.
- `tvb_composite_finalize` and `tvb_free_chain` will both attempt to free the same memory.
- Wireshark will crash due to the double-free.

Fix
