The Vulnerability
[Optional] CWE/CVE Number and description:
CWE-787: Out-of-bounds Write

[Mandatory] Summary:
The vulnerability is in the `capture_ws_check_packet` function in `src/capture.c`. It can be triggered when processing a specially crafted WebSocket packet. The function fails to adequately validate the packet's payload length against the size of the received packet before reading extended payload lengths and masking keys, leading to out-of-bounds memory reads and a subsequent out-of-bounds write during payload unmasking.

[Mandatory] Root cause:
Insufficient validation of WebSocket packet payload length fields before reading header data.

