The Vulnerability
[Optional] CWE/CVE Number and description:
CWE-416: Use After Free
[Mandatory] Summary:
A use-after-free vulnerability exists in the `io_poll_update` function within the Linux kernel's io_uring subsystem. The function manipulates a poll request (`preq`) after it has potentially been freed by `io_poll_disarm`. If a concurrent operation frees the request after it is disarmed but before it is accessed again, it can lead to a use-after-free condition, which is exploitable for privilege escalation.
[Mandatory] Root cause:
The `preq` object is accessed after `io_poll_disarm` potentially frees it, without proper synchronization to prevent concurrent access and freeing.
[Mandatory] Attack Surface:
Kernel driver (io_uring subsystem)
[Mandatory] Impact Summary:
Local privilege escalation
[Optional] Trigger / Attack vector:
io_uring poll update request
