The Vulnerability
[Optional] CWE/CVE Number and description:
CWE-416: Use After Free
[Mandatory] Summary:
The vulnerability exists in the Py_FindObjects function within scipy/ndimage/src/nd_image.c. If an error occurs after a result list is allocated, the `goto exit` cleanup path is taken. On this path, if a Python exception is set, the code returns NULL but previously decremented the reference count of the already-incremented result object, leading to a use-after-free when the Python garbage collector eventually accesses the freed memory.
[Mandatory] Root cause:
A superfluous `Py_XDECREF(result)` call in the error path decrements a reference count that was previously incremented for the return value.
[Mandatory] Attack Surface:
Local Python process executing a crafted call to the `scipy.ndimage.find_objects` function.
[Mandatory] Impact Summary:
Application crash or potential arbitrary code execution via use-after-free.
[Optional] Trigger / Attack vector:
A malicious script or user input that causes `Py_FindObjects` to fail after it has successfully allocated and incremented the result object.
[Mandatory] Key code/struct excerpt (minimal):

exit:
    Py_XDECREF(input);
    Py_XDECREF(result);
    Py_XDECREF(tuple);
    Py_XDECREF(start);
    Py_XDECREF(end);
    Py_XDECREF(slc);
    free(regions);
    if (PyErr_Occurred()) {
        return NULL;
    } else {
        return result;
    }

