The Vulnerability
[Optional] CWE/CVE Number and description:
CWE-787
[Mandatory] Summary:
A use-after-free vulnerability exists in the binder IPC driver's transaction cleanup logic. When releasing an outdated transaction buffer, the function `binder_transaction_buffer_release` was called with a `failed_at` argument of zero, which caused it to incorrectly release all objects in the buffer. This premature freeing of nodes could lead to their subsequent use, resulting in a use-after-free condition, as seen in `binder_proc_transaction` when handling outdated transactions.
[Mandatory] Root cause:
Incorrect interpretation of a zero `failed_at` offset in `binder_transaction_buffer_release`, leading to premature freeing of buffer objects.
[Mandatory] Attack Surface:
Kernel driver (Android Binder IPC)
[Mandatory] Impact Summary:
Local privilege escalation
[Optional] Trigger / Attack vector:
Not available in input
