[Mandatory] Fix summary:
The patch replaces the call to `binder_transaction_buffer_release(proc, NULL, buffer, 0, 0)` with `binder_release_entire_buffer(proc, NULL, buffer, false)`. This change ensures that the buffer cleanup logic correctly handles the release of outdated transaction buffers without misinterpreting the `failed_at` offset, thus preventing the use-after-free.

