The Vulnerability
[Optional] CWE/CVE Number and description:
CWE-125
[Mandatory] Summary:
The bug is in the `ksmbd_conn_handler_loop` function in `fs/smb/server/connection.c`. It is triggered when an attacker sends a malicious SMB packet with a NetBIOS length field (`pdu_size`) that is less than the minimum required SMB header size. The code allocates a buffer based on this small size, but subsequent processing reads the SMB command from a fixed offset (`conn->request_buf + 12`), leading to an out-of-bounds read.
[Mandatory] Root cause:
The NetBIOS `pdu_size` field is not validated against the minimum SMB header size before allocation and use.
[Mandatory] Attack Surface:
Network service (ksmbd SMB server)
[Mandatory] Impact Summary:
Kernel information leak or potential denial of service due to out-of-bounds read.
[Optional] Trigger / Attack vector:
Specially crafted SMB packet sent over the network.
[Mandatory] Key code/struct excerpt (minimal):
