Network packet (SMB over TCP)

[Mandatory] Exploit primitive(s) available:
Out-of-bounds read

[Mandatory] Exploitability summary (1 sentence):
The exploit is easy to trigger as it only requires sending a single network packet with a small length value, potentially leading to information disclosure or a crash.

[Mandatory] Exploit script (summary, 3—6 bullets):
- Connect to the target ksmbd server.
- Send a NetBIOS session message with a length field in the header set to 0.
- The server will allocate a small buffer (5 bytes) for the request.
- The server will then attempt to read the SMB command from a fixed offset beyond the buffer's end.
- This results in an out-of-bounds memory read, which may crash the kernel or leak memory.

Fix
[Mandatory] Fix code:
