[Mandatory] ID:
CVE-2023-3609

[Mandatory] Title: CVE-2023-3609 / CWE-416:
Use After Free

[Optional] Disclosure / Patch Dates:
Initial advisory: 2023-07-21 — Patch release: 2023-07-21

[Optional] Affected products/versions:
Linux Kernel (pre-commit 04c55383fa5689357bcdd2c8036725a55ed632bc)

The Vulnerability
[Optional] CWE/CVE Number and description:
CWE-416: Use After Free
[Mandatory] Summary:
In the `u32_set_parms` function within the Linux kernel's traffic control (`cls_u32`) module, a reference counter for a hash table (`ht_down`) is incremented before a subsequent, potentially failing operation (`tcf_change_indev`). If this operation fails, the function returns early without decrementing the reference counter. This can lead to a mismatched reference count, premature freeing of the object, and a use-after-free condition when the freed object is later accessed, potentially leading to privilege escalation.
[Mandatory] Root cause:
An early return from `u32_set_parms` on failure of `tcf_change_indev` without decrementing a previously incremented reference counter.
[Mandatory] Attack Surface:
Kernel network subsystem (traffic classifier configuration via netlink).
[Mandatory] Impact Summary:
Local Privilege Escalation
[Optional] Trigger / Attack vector:
Netlink message configuring a u32 traffic classifier with a specific attribute that triggers a failure.
