The Vulnerability
[Optional] CWE/CVE Number and description:
CWE-416: Use After Free
[Mandatory] Summary:
The bug is in the `nfc_llcp_mac_is_up` function in `net/nfc/llcp_core.c`. The function calls `nfc_llcp_find_local` to get a `local` object but fails to release its reference on all exit paths, leading to a use-after-free. This is exploitable because the reference leak allows the `local` object to be freed while still in use, as shown by the missing `nfc_llcp_local_put(local)` call before an early return.
[Mandatory] Root cause:
Missing reference release (`nfc_llcp_local_put`) on an early exit path.
