The Vulnerability
[Optional] CWE/CVE Number and description:
 Improper Restriction of Operations within the Bounds of a Memory Buffer
[Mandatory] Summary:
 A bug in the H.264 decoder function `ih264d_parse_islice_data_cabac` leads to an incorrect macroblock count. The counter `ps_dec->u2_total_mbs_coded` is incremented per-macroblock instead of per-group, causing a mismatch between the expected and actual number of processed macroblocks. This discrepancy can corrupt internal state, leading to memory corruption when processing a crafted video stream.
[Mandatory] Root cause:
 The total macroblock counter `ps_dec->u2_total_mbs_coded` is incremented inside the main loop for each macroblock, rather than after a group of macroblocks is processed.
[Mandatory] Attack Surface:
H.264 video stream decoder
[Mandatory] Impact Summary:
Memory corruption leading to potential Remote Code Execution
[Optional] Trigger / Attack vector:
Crafted H.264 video file
[Mandatory] Key code/struct excerpt (minimal):
