annotation:
[Mandatory] ID:
CVE-2016-0816

[Mandatory] Title: CVE-2016-0816 / CWE-119:
Improper Restriction of Operations within the Bounds of a Memory Buffer

[Optional] Disclosure / Patch Dates:
Initial advisory: 2016-03-12 — Patch release: Not available in input

[Optional] Affected products/versions:
Not available in input

The Vulnerability
[Optional] CWE/CVE Number and description:
Improper Restriction of Operations within the Bounds of a Memory Buffer
[Mandatory] Summary:
The bug is in the `ih264d_mark_err_slice_skip` function where the total macroblock count (`ps_dec->u2_total_mbs_coded`) is incremented per macroblock instead of per group of processed macroblocks. This can lead to an incorrect count that does not reflect the actual state of the decoder's macroblock map, potentially causing out-of-bounds memory operations when the count is used as a boundary.
[Mandatory] Root cause:
The macroblock count is updated with the wrong granularity, incrementing per macroblock rather than after processing a batch.
[Mandatory] Attack Surface:
H.264 video decoder
[Mandatory] Impact Summary:
Memory corruption → Remote Code Execution
[Optional] Trigger / Attack vector:
Malicious H.264 video stream
[Mandatory] Key code/struct excerpt (minimal):
    while(!u1_slice_end)
    {
        ...
        i2_cur_mb_addr++;
        u1_num_mbs++;
        ps_dec->u2_total_mbs_coded++;
        u1_num_mbsNby2++;
        ps_parse_mb_data++;

Exploit:

[Mandatory] Trigger surface/attack vector:
Malicious H.264 video stream

[Mandatory] Exploit primitive(s) available:
Out-of-bounds write

[Mandatory] Exploitability summary (1 sentence):
Controlled data in the video stream can lead to an inconsistent state, enabling an attacker to corrupt memory.

[Mandatory] Exploit script (summary, 3—6 bullets):
- Craft an H.264 video stream that triggers the error handling path in `ih264d_mark_err_slice_skip`.
- Manipulate slice parameters to cause the decoder to enter the vulnerable loop.
- The incorrect macroblock count leads to a write past the allocated buffer.
- This results in memory corruption, potentially leading to code execution.

Fix
[Mandatory] Fix code:
    if(u1_decode_nmb)
    {
        ps_dec->pf_mvpred_ref_tfr_nby2mb(ps_dec, u1_mb_idx, u1_num_mbs);
        u1_num_mbsNby2 = 0;

        ps_parse_mb_data = ps_dec->ps_parse_mb_data;
        ps_dec->ps_part = ps_dec->ps_parse_part_params;

        if(ps_dec->u1_separate_parse)
        {
            ih264d_parse_tfr_nmb(ps_dec, u1_mb_idx, u1_num_mbs,
                                 u1_num_mbs_next, u1_tfr_n_mb, u1_end_of_row);
            ps_dec->ps_nmb_info +=  u1_num_mbs;
        }
        else
        {
            ih264d_decode_recon_tfr_nmb(ps_dec, u1_mb_idx, u1_num_mbs, u1_num_mbs_next,
                                        u1_tfr_n_mb, u1_end_of_row);
        }
        ps_dec->u2_total_mbs_coded += u1_num_mbs;
        if(u1_tfr_n_mb)
            u1_num_mbs = 0;
        u1_mb_idx = u1_num_mbs;
        ps_dec->u1_mb_idx = u1_num_mbs;
    }

[Mandatory] Fix summary:
The patch updates the total macroblock count after a group of macroblocks is processed, not after each individual macroblock, ensuring the count remains consistent with the decoder's state.
[Optional] Patch reference:
https://android.googlesource.com/platform/external/libavc/+/4a524d3a8ae9aa20c36430008e6bd429443f8f1d
[Optional] Patch Analysis:
What did the fix do?
- Field: PatchType (e.g., bounds check added, logic refactor, feature removal)
Logic refactor: The fix moves the increment of `ps_dec->u2_total_mbs_coded` to occur after processing a batch of macroblocks, correcting the update logic.
[Optional] Variant & Triage Guidance

[Optional] Variant analysis suggestions (2—3 bullets):
- Review other functions in the decoder that update macroblock counts to ensure they use the correct granularity.
- Fuzz the H.264 parser with streams designed to trigger error-handling paths.
- Diff against similar open-source H.264 decoders to identify analogous patterns.

[Optional] Likely variants/impact (one line):
Similar counting errors could exist in other parts of the decoder leading to memory corruption.

