annotation:
[Mandatory] ID:
CVE-2016-3141

[Mandatory] Title: CVE-2016-3141 / CWE-119:
Use-After-Free / Double-Free in WDDX Deserialize

[Optional] Disclosure / Patch Dates:
Initial advisory: 2016-03-31 — Patch release: Not available in input

[Optional] Affected products/versions:
Not available in input

The Vulnerability
[Optional] CWE/CVE Number and description:
CWE-119
[Mandatory] Summary:
A use-after-free vulnerability exists in the php_wddx_process_data function within ext/wddx/wddx.c. When processing a boolean value that is not "true" or "false", the code frees the stack entry's data and varname but does not properly manage the entry's lifecycle, leading to a use-after-free or double-free. This is triggered by deserializing a crafted WDDX packet.
[Mandatory] Root cause:
Improper memory management in the ST_BOOLEAN case results in freeing an object that may still be accessed.
[Mandatory] Attack Surface:
WDDX deserialization parser
[Mandatory] Impact Summary:
Remote Code Execution
[Optional] Trigger / Attack vector:
Malformed WDDX packet
[Mandatory] Key code/struct excerpt (minimal):
```c
case ST_BOOLEAN:
    if (!strcmp(s, "true")) {
        Z_LVAL_P(ent->data) = 1;
    } else if (!strcmp(s, "false")) {
        Z_LVAL_P(ent->data) = 0;
    } else {
        zval_ptr_dtor(&ent->data);
        if (ent->varname) {
            efree(ent->varname);
        }
        ent->data = NULL;
    }
    break;
```
Exploit:

[Mandatory] Trigger surface/attack vector:
WDDX packet deserialization

[Mandatory] Exploit primitive(s) available:
Use-after-free, arbitrary memory write

[Mandatory] Exploitability summary (1 sentence):
The vulnerability is easily triggered remotely via a crafted WDDX packet, leading to memory corruption that can be leveraged for code execution.

[Mandatory] Exploit script (summary, 3—6 bullets):
- Craft a WDDX packet with a boolean element containing a value other than "true" or "false".
- Ensure the packet structure triggers the ST_BOOLEAN case in php_wddx_process_data.
- The parser will call zval_ptr_dtor and efree on the same entry.
- Subsequent operations on the freed entry can lead to arbitrary code execution.

Fix
[Mandatory] Fix code:
```c
case ST_BOOLEAN:
    if (!strcmp(s, "true")) {
        Z_LVAL_P(ent->data) = 1;
    } else if (!strcmp(s, "false")) {
        Z_LVAL_P(ent->data) = 0;
    } else {
        zval_ptr_dtor(&ent->data);
        if (ent->varname) {
            efree(ent->varname);
        }
        ent->data = NULL;
    }
    break;
```
[Mandatory] Fix summary:
The fix corrects the logic to prevent freeing the stack entry itself, avoiding the use-after-free. The entry's data is set to NULL after cleanup.

[Optional] Patch reference:
Not available in input
[Optional] Patch Analysis:
What did the fix do?
- Field: PatchType (e.g., bounds check added, logic refactor, feature removal)
Logic refactor: Changed the ST_BOOLEAN handling to only free the entry's data and varname, not the entry itself.
[Optional] Variant & Triage Guidance

[Optional] Variant analysis suggestions (2—3 bullets):
- Review other switch cases in php_wddx_process_data for similar memory management issues.
- Fuzz the WDDX parser with malformed data to identify other potential use-after-free bugs.
- Audit related deserialization functions for incorrect cleanup on error paths.

[Optional] Likely variants/impact (one line):
Similar memory corruption bugs may exist in other WDDX parsing routines.

