[Mandatory] ID: CVE-2016-3142

[Mandatory] Title: CVE-2016-3142 / CWE-119: Out-of-Bound Read

[Optional] Disclosure / Patch Dates:
Initial advisory: 2016-03-31 — Patch release: Not available in input

[Optional] Affected products/versions:
Not available in input

The Vulnerability
[Optional] CWE/CVE Number and description:
CWE-119

[Mandatory] Summary:
An out-of-bounds read vulnerability exists in the phar_zip_flush function within ext/phar/zip.c. The bug is triggered when processing a specially crafted PHAR archive, potentially leading to information disclosure. The issue is related to improper bounds checking during the handling of the stub or metadata, as indicated by the commit message referencing an out-of-bounds read in a related parsing function.

[Mandatory] Root cause:
Improper validation of data length or offset leading to an out-of-bounds read operation.

[Mandatory] Attack Surface:
File parsing (PHAR archive processing)

[Mandatory] Impact Summary:
Information disclosure

[Optional] Trigger / Attack vector:
Specially crafted PHAR archive file

[Mandatory] Key code/struct excerpt (minimal):
```c
strncpy(eocd.signature, "PK\5\6", 4);
if (!phar->is_data && !phar->sig_flags) {
    phar->sig_flags = PHAR_SIG_SHA1;
}
if (phar->sig_flags) {
    PHAR_SET_16(eocd.counthere, zend_hash_num_elements(&phar->manifest) + 1);
