[Mandatory] ID: CVE-2016-2857

[Mandatory] Title: CVE-2016-2857 / CWE-119:
packet payload length

[Optional] Disclosure / Patch Dates:
Initial advisory: 2016-04-12 — Patch release: Not available in input

[Optional] Affected products/versions:
Not available in input

The Vulnerability
[Optional] CWE/CVE Number and description:
Improper Restriction of Operations within the Bounds of a Memory Buffer
[Mandatory] Summary:
The vulnerability exists in the `net_checksum_calculate` function in `net/checksum.c`. It is triggered when processing a network packet where the calculated IP payload length (`plen`) is larger than the actual size of the input buffer (`length`). The code fails to validate this condition before writing the calculated checksum to memory, leading to an out-of-bounds write.
[Mandatory] Root cause:
The function lacked a sufficient bounds check to ensure that the calculated end of the packet payload did not exceed the supplied buffer size.
[Mandatory] Attack Surface:
Network service
[Mandatory] Impact Summary:
Local information leak and potential denial of service
[Optional] Trigger / Attack vector:
Crafted network packet
[Mandatory] Key code/struct excerpt (minimal):
    hlen  = (data[14] & 0x0f) * 4;
    plen  = (data[16] << 8 | data[17]) - hlen;
    proto = data[23];

    switch (proto) {
    case PROTO_TCP:
