    data[14+hlen+csum_offset+1] = 0;
Exploit:

[Mandatory] Trigger surface/attack vector:
Crafted network packet

[Mandatory] Exploit primitive(s) available:
Out-of-bounds write

[Mandatory] Exploitability summary (1 sentence):
The exploit is triggered by sending a packet with a manipulated payload length field that passes existing minimal checks, leading to a controlled out-of-bounds write.

[Mandatory] Exploit script (summary, 3—6 bullets):
- Attacker crafts a network packet with a valid L2 and L3 header.
- The IPv4 total length field is set to a value larger than the actual packet buffer size.
- This results in a calculated `plen` that, when combined with the header length (`hlen`), exceeds the `length` argument.
- The function proceeds to write the computed checksum past the end of the `data` buffer.
- This results in an out-of-bounds memory write.

Fix
[Mandatory] Fix code:
    /* Ensure data has complete L2 & L3 headers. */
    if (length < 14 + 20) {
        return;
    }

    if ((data[14] & 0xf0) != 0x40)
