The Vulnerability
[Optional] CWE/CVE Number and description:
Improper Restriction of Operations within the Bounds of a Memory Buffer
[Mandatory] Summary:
The vulnerability exists in the WT_VoiceFilter function within eas_wtengine.c. The function processes audio samples based on the numSamples field from the pWTIntFrame structure without validating that it is positive. This allows a negative or zero value to be passed, which can cause the while loop to underflow, leading to an out-of-bounds write to the pAudioBuffer. This is exploitable because an attacker can control the input frame data, triggering the memory corruption.
[Mandatory] Root cause:
The root cause is the lack of a sanity check on the numSamples field before it is used to control the loop count.
[Mandatory] Attack Surface:
Local application processing malicious audio data.
[Mandatory] Impact Summary:
Memory corruption → Potential Code Execution
