annotation:
[Mandatory] ID:
CVE-2016-0841

[Mandatory] Title: CVE-2016-0841 / CWE-119:
Use of cleared service binder

[Optional] Disclosure / Patch Dates:
Initial advisory: 2016-04-18 — Patch release: Not available in input

[Optional] Affected products/versions:
Not available in input

The Vulnerability
[Optional] CWE/CVE Number and description:
CWE-119
[Mandatory] Summary:
The bug is in the `MediaMetadataRetriever` constructor where a reference to a service binder is obtained. If the service binder is cleared after the reference is taken but before it is used, the program can operate on a stale or invalid object. This is exploitable because it can lead to use-after-free conditions, potentially allowing for arbitrary code execution.
[Mandatory] Root cause:
A reference to a potentially transient service binder is stored and used, allowing for a use-after-free if the binder is cleared.
[Mandatory] Attack Surface:
Local application framework (media service interaction)
[Mandatory] Impact Summary:
Local privilege escalation
[Optional] Trigger / Attack vector:
Not available in input
[Mandatory] Key code/struct excerpt (minimal):
MediaMetadataRetriever::MediaMetadataRetriever()
{
    ALOGV("constructor");
    const sp<IMediaPlayerService>& service(getService());
    if (service == 0) {
        ALOGE("failed to obtain MediaMetadataRetrieverService");
        return;
    }
    sp<IMediaMetadataRetriever> retriever(service->createMetadataRetriever());
    if (retriever == 0) {
        ALOGE("failed to create IMediaMetadataRetriever object from server");
    }
    mRetriever = retriever;
}

