Fix
[Mandatory] Fix code:
MediaMetadataRetriever::MediaMetadataRetriever()
{
    ALOGV("constructor");
    const sp<IMediaPlayerService> service(getService());
    if (service == 0) {
        ALOGE("failed to obtain MediaMetadataRetrieverService");
        return;
    }
    sp<IMediaMetadataRetriever> retriever(service->createMetadataRetriever());
    if (retriever == 0) {
        ALOGE("failed to create IMediaMetadataRetriever object from server");
    }
    mRetriever = retriever;
}

[Mandatory] Fix summary:
The patch changed the service variable to be obtained by value instead of by reference, preventing a cleared service binder from being used.

[Optional] Patch reference:
https://android.googlesource.com/platform/frameworks/av/+/3097f364237fb552871f7639d37a7afa4563e252
[Optional] Patch Analysis:
What did the fix do?
- Field: PatchType (bounds check added, logic refactor, feature removal): logic refactor
[Optional] Variant & Triage Guidance

[Optional] Variant analysis suggestions (2—3 bullets):
- Review other locations in the codebase where service binders are obtained by reference.
- Fuzz media service interactions to find similar use-after-free conditions.
- Diff forks of the Android framework for similar patterns.

[Optional] Likely variants/impact (one line):
Similar use-after-free bugs may exist where binders are passed by reference.

