[Mandatory] ID:
CVE-2014-9765

[Mandatory] Title: CVE-2014-9765 / CWE-119:
Buffer overflow in appheader parser

[Optional] Disclosure / Patch Dates:
Initial advisory: 2016-04-19 — Patch release: Not available in input

[Optional] Affected products/versions:
jmacd/xdelta-gpl (pre-commit ef93ff74203e030073b898c05e8b4860b5d09ef2)

The Vulnerability
[Optional] CWE/CVE Number and description:
CWE-119
[Mandatory] Summary:
A buffer overflow vulnerability exists in the `main_get_appheader` function when parsing an application header. The code iterates through a string, splitting it by '/' delimiters and storing pointers into a fixed-size array `parsed`. The loop condition fails to check if the array index `place` exceeds the bounds of `parsed`, allowing an out-of-bounds write. This can be triggered by a crafted input with more than four '/'-separated arguments.
[Mandatory] Root cause:
The `while` loop condition does not check the array bounds before writing to `parsed[place++]`.
[Mandatory] Attack Surface:
Network service or file parser processing xdelta3 application headers.
[Mandatory] Impact Summary:
Memory corruption → Potential Remote Code Execution
[Optional] Trigger / Attack vector:
A specially crafted xdelta3 file or stream containing an application header with more than four arguments.
[Mandatory] Key code/struct excerpt (minimal):
      char *start = (char*)apphead;
      char *slash;
      int   place = 0;
