The Vulnerability
[Optional] CWE/CVE Number and description:
Improper Restriction of Operations within the Bounds of a Memory Buffer (CWE-119)

[Mandatory] Summary:
The vulnerability exists in the `btif_dm_pin_reply` function in `btif/src/btif_dm.c`. The function accepts a PIN code length (`pin_len`) from a remote client without validating that it is within the bounds of the `pin_code` buffer. This allows a malicious client to specify a large `pin_len`, leading to an out-of-bounds write when the PIN code is processed, as shown in the code excerpt where the length is passed to `BTA_DmPinReply` without sufficient checks.

[Mandatory] Root cause:
The function failed to validate that the supplied `pin_len` parameter was less than or equal to the maximum PIN code length (`PIN_CODE_LEN`).

[Mandatory] Attack Surface:
Bluetooth stack (via remote device pairing)

[Mandatory] Impact Summary:
Remote code execution or denial of service via memory corruption.

[Optional] Trigger / Attack vector:
Malicious Bluetooth device during pairing with a long PIN code.

