[Mandatory] Summary:
The bug is in the `r_egg_compile` function in `libr/egg/egg.c`. It processes input bytes in a loop, calling `r_egg_lang_parsechar` for each byte. The function lacks a bounds check on `egg->lang.elem_n` before it is incremented, allowing it to grow beyond the size of the fixed-size `egg->lang.elem` buffer. This can lead to an out-of-bounds write, which is exploitable when processing specially crafted input.
