					} else {
						if (k < NEWSTR_SIZE - 1) {
							newstr[k] = ops[i].str[j];
						} else {
							newstr[k] = '\0';
							return false;
						}
					}
				}
```
[Mandatory] Fix summary:
 The patch adds bounds checking before copying strings into the `newstr` buffer, preventing an overflow by ensuring there is enough space remaining. It replaces `strcpy` with a safer `memcpy` and checks the buffer size on each iteration.

