[Mandatory] ID:
CVE-2019-12865

[Mandatory] Title: CVE-2019-12865 / CWE-415:
Double-free in ms command

[Optional] Disclosure / Patch Dates:
Initial advisory: 2019-06-17 — Patch release: Not available in input

[Optional] Affected products/versions:
radare2 (pre-commit 40453029179d230cf02ffed205f2d63e33981b8f)

The Vulnerability
[Optional] CWE/CVE Number and description:
Double Free

[Mandatory] Summary:
The vulnerability is in the `cmd_mount` function within `libr/core/cmd_mount.c`. When handling the 's' command (ms), the code allocates memory for `cwd` and later frees it using `free(cwd)`. However, the `R_FREE` macro is used elsewhere to safely free memory and set the pointer to NULL. The direct use of `free` leads to a double-free condition if the pointer is freed again elsewhere, causing a crash or potential memory corruption.

[Mandatory] Root cause:
The code calls `free(cwd)` directly instead of using the `R_FREE` macro, which nulls the pointer after freeing, leading to a potential double-free.

[Mandatory] Attack Surface:
Command-line interface of radare2 (ms command)

[Mandatory] Impact Summary:
Application crash / Denial of Service

[Optional] Trigger / Attack vector:
Specially crafted command sequence in the radare2 shell to trigger the 'ms' command path.

[Mandatory] Key code/struct excerpt (minimal):
```
		{
			RFSShell shell = {
