			r_pvector_init (&rli->completion.args, free);  // UGLY HACK
			rli->completion.run = ms_autocomplete;
			rli->completion.run_user = rli->user;
			r_line_completion_set (&rli->completion, ms_argc, ms_argv);
			r_fs_shell_prompt (&shell, core->fs, input);
			R_FREE (cwd);
			r_pvector_clear (&rli->completion.args);
			memcpy (&rli->completion, &c, sizeof (c));
		}
```

[Mandatory] Fix summary:
The patch replaces the direct `free(cwd)` call with `R_FREE(cwd)`, which safely frees the memory and nulls the pointer to prevent double-free issues.

[Optional] Patch reference:
Commit 40453029179d230cf02ffed205f2d63e33981b8f

[Optional] Patch Analysis:
- Field: PatchType (bounds check added, logic refactor, feature removal)
What did the fix do?
The fix replaces a direct `free()` call with the `R_FREE()` macro to prevent a double-free vulnerability by ensuring the pointer is set to NULL after being freed.
[Optional] Variant & Triage Guidance

[Optional] Variant analysis suggestions (2—3 bullets):
- Audit the codebase for other direct uses of `free()` where `R_FREE` should be used.
- Fuzz the command-line interface to trigger other potential memory management errors.
- Review all command handlers in `cmd_mount.c` for similar unsafe memory handling patterns.

[Optional] Likely variants/impact (one line):
Other commands may have similar double-free issues if they misuse `free()`.

