[Mandatory] ID:
CVE-2019-13297

[Mandatory] Title: CVE-2019-13297 / CWE-125:
Out-of-bounds read in AdaptiveThresholdImage

[Optional] Disclosure / Patch Dates:
Initial advisory: 2019-07-05 — Patch release: Not available in input

[Optional] Affected products/versions:
ImageMagick/ImageMagick6 (pre-35c7032723d85eee7318ff6c82f031fa2666b773)

The Vulnerability
[Optional] CWE/CVE Number and description:
CWE-125: Out-of-bounds Read
[Mandatory] Summary:
The vulnerability exists in the AdaptiveThresholdImage function in magick/threshold.c. The function fails to validate that the height parameter is non-zero before proceeding with calculations, leading to an out-of-bounds read when processing image pixels. This occurs because the code only checks if width is zero, allowing an invalid height to cause a division by zero and subsequent memory access errors.
[Mandatory] Root cause:
The height parameter is not checked for a zero value before being used in calculations, leading to a division by zero and out-of-bounds read.
[Mandatory] Attack Surface:
Image processing library function
[Mandatory] Impact Summary:
Information leak / potential denial of service
[Optional] Trigger / Attack vector:
Specially crafted image file or API call invoking AdaptiveThresholdImage with a height of zero

[Mandatory] Key code/struct excerpt (minimal):
  if (image->debug != MagickFalse)
    (void) LogMagickEvent(TraceEvent,GetMagickModule(),"%s",image->filename);
  assert(exception != (ExceptionInfo *) NULL);
  assert(exception->signature == MagickCoreSignature);
  threshold_image=CloneImage(image,0,0,MagickTrue,exception);
  if (threshold_image == (Image *) NULL)
    return((Image *) NULL);
  if (width == 0)
    return(threshold_image);
  if (SetImageStorageClass(threshold_image,DirectClass) == MagickFalse)
    {
      InheritException(exception,&threshold_image->exception);
      threshold_image=DestroyImage(threshold_image);
      return((Image *) NULL);
    }

Exploit:

[Mandatory] Trigger surface/attack vector:
API call to AdaptiveThresholdImage or processing a crafted image

[Mandatory] Exploit primitive(s) available:
Out-of-bounds read

[Mandatory] Exploitability summary (1 sentence):
The vulnerability is easily triggered by passing a zero value for the height parameter, leading to predictable memory access violations.

[Mandatory] Exploit script (summary, 3—6 bullets):
- Invoke AdaptiveThresholdImage with a valid image pointer.
- Set the width parameter to a non-zero value.
- Set the height parameter to zero.
- The function will proceed without returning early, leading to a division by zero in the number_pixels calculation.
- This results in an out-of-bounds read when accessing pixel data.

Fix
[Mandatory] Fix code:
  if (image->debug != MagickFalse)
    (void) LogMagickEvent(TraceEvent,GetMagickModule(),"%s",image->filename);
  assert(exception != (ExceptionInfo *) NULL);
  assert(exception->signature == MagickCoreSignature);
  threshold_image=CloneImage(image,0,0,MagickTrue,exception);
  if (threshold_image == (Image *) NULL)
    return((Image *) NULL);
  if ((width == 0) || (height == 0))
    return(threshold_image);
  if (SetImageStorageClass(threshold_image,DirectClass) == MagickFalse)
    {
      InheritException(exception,&threshold_image->exception);
      threshold_image=DestroyImage(threshold_image);
      return((Image *) NULL);
    }

[Mandatory] Fix summary:
The fix adds a check for the height parameter being zero, ensuring the function returns early if either width or height is invalid, preventing the division by zero and out-of-bounds read.

[Optional] Patch reference:
Commit 35c7032723d85eee7318ff6c82f031fa2666b773
[Optional] Patch Analysis:
What did the fix do?
- Field: PatchType (bounds check added)
[Optional] Variant & Triage Guidance

[Optional] Variant analysis suggestions (2—3 bullets):
- Review other image processing functions for similar missing parameter validations.
- Fuzz the AdaptiveThresholdImage function with various width and height values to ensure no other edge cases exist.
- Examine functions that perform calculations based on width and height to ensure all are validated against zero.

[Optional] Likely variants/impact (one line):
Other functions in the image processing library may have similar missing validation for zero-valued dimensions.

