[Mandatory] ID:
CVE-2019-13308

[Mandatory] Title: CVE-2019-13308 / CWE-787:
Out-of-bounds write

[Optional] Disclosure / Patch Dates:
Initial advisory: [2019-07-05] — Patch release: [2019-07-05]

[Optional] Affected products/versions:
ImageMagick (pre-commit 61135001a625364e29bdce83832f043eebde7b5a)

The Vulnerability
[Optional] CWE/CVE Number and description:
CWE-787: Out-of-bounds Write
[Mandatory] Summary:
The vulnerability exists in the `ComplexImages` function within `MagickCore/fourier.c`. The function processes image pixels using different complex mathematical operations in a loop. The bug is triggered because the loop bounds and pixel channel counts are incorrectly derived from the input `images` object instead of the destination `Cr_image` object. This mismatch can lead to writing past the allocated memory for the destination image buffers when the source and destination images have different dimensions or channel counts, resulting in an out-of-bounds write.
[Mandatory] Root cause:
Incorrect loop bounds and pixel channel counts derived from the source image (`images`) instead of the destination image (`Cr_image`).
[Mandatory] Attack Surface:
Image processing library (ImageMagick)
[Mandatory] Impact Summary:
Out-of-bounds write → Potential Code Execution
[Optional] Trigger / Attack vector:
Specially crafted image file processed via the ComplexImages function.
[Mandatory] Key code/struct excerpt (minimal):

    for (y=0; y < (ssize_t) images->rows; y++)
    {
      ...
      for (x=0; x < (ssize_t) images->columns; x++)
      {
        ...
        for (i=0; i < (ssize_t) GetPixelChannels(images); i++)
        {
          switch (op)
          {
            case DivideComplexOperator:
            {
              double
                gamma;
              gamma=PerceptibleReciprocal(Br[i]*Br[i]+Bi[i]*Bi[i]+snr);
              Cr[i]=gamma*(Ar[i]*Br[i]+Ai[i]*Bi[i]);
              Ci[i]=gamma*(Ai[i]*Br[i]-Ar[i]*Bi[i]);
              break;
            }
          }
        }
      }
    }

Exploit:

[Mandatory] Trigger surface/attack vector:
Image file format parser (ComplexImages function)

[Mandatory] Exploit primitive(s) available:
Out-of-bounds write

[Mandatory] Exploitability summary (1 sentence):
The vulnerability is easily triggered by processing a malicious image with mismatched dimensions, allowing an attacker to write data past the bounds of an allocated buffer.

[Mandatory] Exploit script (summary, 3—6 bullets):
- Create a sequence of images where the source images (`images`) and the destination complex images (`Cr_image`, `Ci_image`) have different numbers of rows, columns, or pixel channels.
- Invoke the `ComplexImages` function with a `ComplexOperator` (e.g., `DivideComplexOperator`).
- The loop will iterate based on the larger source image dimensions, writing past the end of the smaller destination image's allocated pixel buffer.
- This results in a heap-based buffer overflow, which can be leveraged for further exploitation.
- The overflow is controlled by the pixel data from the input image.

Fix
[Mandatory] Fix code:
