    Cr=QueueCacheViewAuthenticPixels(Cr_view,0,y,Cr_image->columns,1,exception);
    Ci=QueueCacheViewAuthenticPixels(Ci_view,0,y,Ci_image->columns,1,exception);
    ...
    for (x=0; x < (ssize_t) Cr_image->columns; x++)
    {
      ...
      for (i=0; i < (ssize_t) GetPixelChannels(Cr_image); i++)
      {
        switch (op)
        {
          case DivideComplexOperator:
          {
            double
              gamma;
            gamma=PerceptibleReciprocal((double) Br[i]*Br[i]+Bi[i]*Bi[i]+snr);
            Cr[i]=gamma*((double) Ar[i]*Br[i]+(double) Ai[i]*Bi[i]);
            Ci[i]=gamma*((double) Ai[i]*Br[i]-(double) Ar[i]*Bi[i]);
            break;
          }
        }
      }
    }

[Mandatory] Fix summary:
The patch corrects the loop bounds and pixel channel counts to be based on the destination image (`Cr_image`) instead of the input image (`images`), preventing out-of-bounds writes. It also adds explicit casts to `double` for arithmetic operations to ensure correct type promotion.

[Optional] Patch reference:
https://github.com/ImageMagick/ImageMagick/commit/61135001a625364e29bdce83832f043eebde7b5a
[Optional] Patch Analysis:
- Field: PatchType (bounds check added, logic refactor, feature removal)
The fix is a logic refactor that corrects the indices used for iteration and memory access, effectively adding bounds by tying them to the correct buffer's dimensions.
[Optional] Variant & Triage Guidance

[Optional] Variant analysis suggestions (2—3 bullets):
- Review other image processing functions in ImageMagick that iterate over multiple images with potentially mismatched dimensions for similar indexing errors.
- Apply differential fuzzing between versions before and after the fix on the `ComplexImages` function to ensure all related edge cases are covered.
- Audit loops that use `GetPixelChannels` to ensure the correct image object is passed as the argument.

[Optional] Likely variants/impact (one line):
Similar out-of-bounds write vulnerabilities may exist in other multi-image processing functions.

