[Mandatory] ID:
CVE-2019-1010238

[Mandatory] Title: CVE-2019-1010238 / CWE-787:
Out-of-bounds write

[Optional] Disclosure / Patch Dates:
Initial advisory: 2019-07-19 — Patch release: Not available in input

[Optional] Affected products/versions:
Not available in input

The Vulnerability
[Optional] CWE/CVE Number and description:
CWE-787
[Mandatory] Summary:
The vulnerability exists in the `pango_log2vis_get_embedding_levels` function in pango/pango-bidi-type.c. It is triggered when processing text that leads to a loop iteration count (`i`) that is equal to or exceeds the allocated size of the `bidi_types` array (`n_chars`). This results in an out-of-bounds write on the `bidi_types` array during the assignment `bidi_types[i] = char_type`, which is exploitable because the loop condition `p < text + length` does not prevent this overrun.
[Mandatory] Root cause:
The loop condition `p < text + length` allows iterations to continue beyond the allocated size of the `bidi_types` array, leading to an out-of-bounds write.
[Mandatory] Attack Surface:
Text rendering library
[Mandatory] Impact Summary:
Out-of-bounds write
[Optional] Trigger / Attack vector:
Specially crafted text input
[Mandatory] Key code/struct excerpt (minimal):
  for (i = 0, p = text; p < text + length; p = g_utf8_next_char(p), i++)
    {
      gunichar ch = g_utf8_get_char (p);
      FriBidiCharType char_type = fribidi_get_bidi_type (ch);

      if (i == n_chars)
        break;

      bidi_types[i] = char_type;
      ored_types |= char_type;
      if (FRIBIDI_IS_STRONG (char_type))
        anded_strongs &= char_type;
#ifdef USE_FRIBIDI_EX_API
      if (G_UNLIKELY(bidi_types[i] == FRIBIDI_TYPE_ON))
        bracket_types[i] = fribidi_get_bracket (ch);
      else
        bracket_types[i] = FRIBIDI_NO_BRACKET;
#endif
    }
Exploit:

[Mandatory] Trigger surface/attack vector:
Specially crafted text input to a function using the pango library.
[Mandatory] Exploit primitive(s) available:
Out-of-bounds write
[Mandatory] Exploitability summary (1 sentence):
The exploit is controllable via input text but may be limited by memory protection features like ASLR and DEP.
[Mandatory] Exploit script (summary, 3—6 bullets):
- Not available in input

Fix
[Mandatory] Fix code:
  for (i = 0, p = text; p < text + length; p = g_utf8_next_char(p), i++)
    {
      gunichar ch = g_utf8_get_char (p);
      FriBidiCharType char_type = fribidi_get_bidi_type (ch);

      if (i == n_chars)
        break;

      bidi_types[i] = char_type;
      ored_types |= char_type;
      if (FRIBIDI_IS_STRONG (char_type))
        anded_strongs &= char_type;
#ifdef USE_FRIBIDI_EX_API
      if (G_UNLIKELY(bidi_types[i] == FRIBIDI_TYPE_ON))
        bracket_types[i] = fribidi_get_bracket (ch);
      else
        bracket_types[i] = FRIBIDI_NO_BRACKET;
#endif
    }

[Mandatory] Fix summary:
The patch adds a bounds check (`if (i == n_chars) break;`) inside the loop to prevent writing past the end of the allocated array.
[Optional] Patch reference:
https://github.com/GNOME/pango/commit/490f8979a260c16b1df055eab386345da18a2d54
[Optional] Patch Analysis:
What did the fix do?
- Field: PatchType (e.g., bounds check added, logic refactor, feature removal)
Bounds check added
[Optional] Variant & Triage Guidance

[Optional] Variant analysis suggestions (2—3 bullets):
- Review other loops in the codebase that iterate over UTF-8 text and use a separate counter to ensure similar bounds checks are present.
- Fuzz the pango library with malformed or specially crafted text inputs to find potential similar out-of-bounds conditions.
- Audit other functions that allocate buffers based on character count (`g_utf8_strlen`) and then iterate based on byte length.

[Optional] Likely variants/impact (one line):
Similar out-of-bounds write vulnerabilities may exist in other text processing functions.

